t["subzone:ironbeard-s-tomb"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,359,24.600.0,18.241.0,26.196.0,44.153.0,34.143.0",["h"]="75acd9",["n"]="Tumba de Barbaférrea",["s"]="Tumba de Barbaférrea. La Tumba de Barbaférrea es un lugar de enterramiento enano profanado situado al oeste del camino que conduce al norte hacia Dun Modr, en Los Humedales. Marcada por un cementerio al aire libre y una estatua de piedra que le da nombre, la cripta ha caído en desuso a medida que los mocos ácidos invadían el terreno. Los viajeros rara vez ponen un pie en la hondonada a menos que busquen pertenencias perdidas devoradas por el fango. Con vistas a las marismas a lo largo del camino hacia el norte a Dun Modr, la Tumba de Barbaférrea se erige como testimonio de la presencia enana en Los Humedales. Una monumental estatua de piedra, que presumiblemente representa al propio Barbaférrea, vigila el cementerio circundante. Sin embargo, la solemne paz ya no vela este lugar. La cripta subterránea ha sido invadida por completo por cepas de mocos negros y carmesíes, dejando la tumba contaminada. Los enanos ya no traen a sus muertos a este santuario en ruinas, y los pocos valientes que se atreven a perturbar las bóvedas lo hacen principalmente para rebuscar entre los restos digeridos por los limos acechantes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="Seeing a clan hero's final resting place infested by mindless marsh oozes is a bitter disgrace for any dwarf traveling the road toward the Thandol Span."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Very little is recorded about Ironbeard himself, though the massive statue and crypt grounds suggest he was an honored dwarven figure of note in the Wetlands. The monument erected in his likeness watches over the hillside above the cemetery.",["al"]={"ironbeard lore","who is ironbeard","statue identity"},["q"]="Who was Ironbeard?"},{["a"]="The crypt has been completely overrun by acidic black and crimson oozes. With the burial grounds defiled and infested with dangerous slimes, mourning families have ceased bringing their dead here.",["al"]={"why abandoned","oozes in tomb","what happened to the crypt"},["q"]="Why is the tomb abandoned?"},{["a"]="Beyond fighting back the foul infestation, travelers frequently search the tomb's slimes hoping to recover swallowed items, most notably Sida's lost bag.",["al"]={"why go here","sida bag","tomb quests"},["q"]="Why do adventurers explore Ironbeard's Tomb?"},{["a"]="The tomb sits in north-central Wetlands, nestled into the hill just west of the main road heading north toward the dwarven redoubt of Dun Modr.",["al"]={"tomb location","how to get to ironbeard tomb","ironbeard wetlands map"},["q"]="Where is Ironbeard's Tomb located?"}},["kw"]={"crypt","dun modr","graveyard","ironbeard","ironbeard's tomb","oozes","sida","wetlands"},["n"]="Ironbeard's Tomb",["s"]="Ironbeard's Tomb is a defiled dwarven burial site situated west of the road leading north toward Dun Modr in the Wetlands. Marked by an outdoor graveyard and a stone statue of its namesake, the crypt has fallen into disuse as acidic oozes swarm the grounds. Travelers rarely set foot in the hollow unless searching for lost possessions swallowed by the slime.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Overlooking the marshes along the road north to Dun Modr, Ironbeard's Tomb stands as a testament to the dwarven presence in the Wetlands. A monumental stone statue, presumed to depict Ironbeard himself, watches over the surrounding burial plot. Yet solemn peace no longer keeps vigil here. The subterranean crypt has been completely overrun by oozes of various black and crimson strains, leaving the tomb contaminated. Dwarves no longer bring their dead to this ruined sanctuary, and those brave enough to disturb the vaults do so primarily to hunt through the remains digested by the lurking slimes.",["t"]="A Befouled Resting Place"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironclad-cove"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,235,19.576.0,20.553.1,50.256.0,49.204.0,27.252.0,34.197.0",["h"]="bef923",["n"]="Cala del Acorazado",["s"]="Cala del Acorazado. La Cala del Acorazado es una inmensa caverna subterránea oculta bajo Páramos de Poniente que alberga un astillero y un muelle subterráneos. Sirve como dársena secreta de construcción para el gran acorazado de la Hermandad Defias y conecta directamente con el mar. Enterrada en el punto más profundo de Las Minas de la Muerte, la Cala del Acorazado es una monumental caverna marina convertida en un astillero fortificado. Aquí, Edwin VanCleef y la Hermandad Defias han construido un enorme buque de guerra conocido como el acorazado. La caverna cuenta con extensos andamios de madera, islotes y pasarelas de carga tripuladas por piratas Defias, marineros y capataces. Su existencia revela la verdadera magnitud de la amenaza Defias: VanCleef no solo pretende asaltar las granjas de Páramos de Poniente, sino reunir una fuerza naval privada capaz de bombardear las mismísimas costas de Ventormenta.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The cove represents the zenith of Edwin VanCleef's craftsmanship, engineering prowess, and underground logistics, making it legendary among thieves and outlaws.",["faction:Alliance"]="Finding a full-sized war galleon buried under Westfall transforms the Defias from a regional bandit gang into an existential military threat against the Kingdom of Stormwind."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The juggernaught is the centerpiece of Edwin VanCleef's military ambitions. The Defias Brotherhood assembled this massive warship deep beneath the earth so it could launch undetected through subterranean water channels and strike at Stormwind from the sea.",["al"]={"why is there a ship here","what is the juggernaught","deadmines ship purpose"},["q"]="What is the ship in Ironclad Cove being built for?"},{["a"]="The massive gates open directly into the ocean along the southern coast of Westfall, near the border of northern Stranglethorn Vale. When opened, the juggernaught can sail straight out into the Great Sea.",["al"]={"where do the sea gates open","deadmines iron doors","exit into the ocean"},["q"]="Where does the large metal door in the cove lead?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood holds the cove under the command of Edwin VanCleef. While independent pirates originally used the secluded cavern, VanCleef's forces wiped them out to commandeer the docks and keep the juggernaught's construction entirely secret.",["al"]={"who runs the cove","who lives in ironclad cove"},["q"]="Who controls Ironclad Cove?"},{["a"]="That is Cookie, the Defias ship's cook. Armed with a rolling pin and cooking cauldrons, he is an unusual ally among the human and goblin renegades, having claimed the galley as his personal domain.",["al"]={"cookie the murloc","why is there a murloc pirate","chef cookie"},["q"]="Who is the murloc aboard the ship?"}},["kw"]={"cookie","deadmines ship","defias cove","edwin vancleef","ironclad cove","juggernaught","shipyard"},["n"]="Ironclad Cove",["s"]="Ironclad Cove is a massive subterranean cavern hidden beneath Westfall, housing an underground shipyard and dock. It serves as the secret construction dock for the Defias Brotherhood's war juggernaught and connects directly to the sea.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Buried at the deepest point of the Deadmines, Ironclad Cove is a monumental sea cavern converted into a fortified dockyard. Here, Edwin VanCleef and the Defias Brotherhood have constructed an enormous warship known as the juggernaught. The cavern features extensive wooden scaffolding, islets, and loading catwalks manned by Defias pirates, deckhands, and overseers. Its existence reveals the true scale of the Defias threat: VanCleef intends not merely to raid Westfall's farmsteads, but to assemble a private naval force capable of bombarding the shores of Stormwind itself.",["t"]="The Hidden Shipyard"},{["b"]="The cavern is dominated by colossal iron-reinforced sea doors set into the rock wall. Once opened, these gates provide a direct outlet into the Great Sea, emerging along the coastline just north of Stranglethorn Vale. Before the Defias Brotherhood seized the cove, it was held by an independent pirate crew whom the Brotherhood slaughtered to ensure total secrecy. Shielded from the eyes of the Stormwind naval fleet, the cove provides the Brotherhood an unmonitored lane for moving contraband, staging maritime raids, and preparing their naval assault.",["t"]="Gateway to the Ocean"}}}}}
t["subzone:ironforge-airfield"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="18,304,29.419.0,38.403.0,34.276.0,34.225.0,41.167.0,44.184.0",["h"]="288c7a",["n"]="Aeródromo de Forjaz",["s"]="Aeródromo de Forjaz. Escondida en lo alto de los picos nevados al noreste de Forjaz, esta remota pista de aterrizaje enana sirve como campo de pruebas y zona de operaciones para las máquinas voladoras de los gnomos y los montañeros enanos. Sin caminos principales que la señalen, la meseta se alza sobre los riscos escarpados de Dun Morogh y el pronunciado descenso hacia Los Humedales. Encaramado muy por encima de los senderos trillados de Dun Morogh, este aeródromo de gran altitud es una discreta maravilla de la cooperación de la Alianza. Al abrigo de las cumbres montañosas circundantes, la cantería enana afianza las crestas azotadas por el viento, mientras que las máquinas voladoras gnomo permanecen estacionadas a lo largo de pistas de aterrizaje al aire libre. Los montañeros vigilan el perímetro junto a ingenieros ocupados en ajustar engranajes e inspeccionar motores que escupen vapor en medio del frío cortante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkers, the airstrip showcases the apex of gnomish aviation, featuring fully assembled flying machines stationed in extreme, sub-zero conditions.",["race:Dwarf"]="A testament to dwarven territorial watchfulness, the airfield proves that Ironforge's Mountaineers stand sentry even in the most inaccessible heights of Khaz Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="There are no roads, flights, or maintained tunnels connecting the valley to Ironforge or lower Dun Morogh. Reaching it requires scaling the steep mountainsides on foot, typically via tricky ridgeline climbing paths beginning out of Loch Modan or near the passes of Dun Morogh.",["al"]={"get to airfield","how to climb to airfield","airfield location","airfield path"},["q"]="How do you get up to the airfield?"},{["a"]="It serves as an elevated flight testing and military outpost where dwarven mountaineers and gnome engineers maintain flying machines and scout the high mountain borderlands separating Dun Morogh, Loch Modan, and the Wetlands.",["al"]={"why is there an airstrip","what is ironforge airfield for"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this place?"},{["a"]="Local Frostmane trolls inhabit caves in the southern cliffs of the valley. Dwarven mountaineers clash regularly with them over the frozen lake just beneath the runway.",["al"]={"who attacks airfield","who is fighting on the lake"},["q"]="Who is attacking the dwarven guards here?"},{["a"]="No standard quests direct adventurers to visit the airstrip in everyday travels. It remains an obscure, remote plateau largely separated from the main logistics of the dwarven kingdom.",["al"]={"any quests here","airfield quests"},["q"]="Is the airfield tied to any official quests?"}},["kw"]={"airfield","airstrip","dun morogh","flying machine","frostmane","ironforge","mountaineers"},["n"]="Ironforge Airfield",["s"]="Tucked away high in the snowy peaks northeast of Ironforge, this remote dwarven airstrip serves as a proving ground and staging area for gnome flying machines and dwarven mountaineers. Unmarked by main roads, the plateau overlooks the jagged crags of Dun Morogh and the steep descent toward the Wetlands.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched far above the beaten trails of Dun Morogh, the high-altitude airfield is a quiet marvel of Alliance cooperation. Sheltered by surrounding mountain peaks, dwarven masonry anchors the blustery ridgelines while gnomish flying machines sit parked along open landing strips. Mountaineers keep watch over the perimeter alongside engineers busy wrenching gears and inspecting steam-belching engines in the biting cold.",["t"]="A Hidden Redoubt in the Crags"},{["b"]="Despite its isolation, the airfield is far from serene. The surrounding valley features frozen waters and crags contested by Frostmane trolls, who dwell in nearby caves and constantly harass the dwarven sentries. In the shadow of the peaks, dwarven defenders and Stormpike patrols clash regularly with troll raiders across the ice, keeping the remote installation in a state of quiet, vigilant standoff.",["t"]="Frontier Skirmishes and Frozen Valleys"}}}}}
t["subzone:ivar-patch"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,241,16.461.0,23.475.1,40.206.0,52.307.0,41.184.0,32.134.0",["h"]="c8c9b0",["n"]="Los Dominios de Ivar",["s"]="Los Dominios de Ivar. Los Dominios de Ivar son una granja de calabazas asolada ubicada en el norte del Bosque de Argénteos. En su día fue una próspera finca agrícola de Lordaeron, pero sus residentes fueron aniquilados durante la Tercera Guerra y transformados en necrófagos voraces y ciegamente hostiles. Antes de que la Tercera Guerra arrasara Lordaeron, este campo de calabazas era una próspera propiedad de un granjero llamado Ivar, quien empleaba a un animado grupo de peones y sirvientes. Cuando la Plaga desató la peste de la no-muerte por la campiña, la granja quedó completamente consumida. En lugar de alzarse con la mente intacta como los Renegados de libre albedrío, Ivar, su familia y sus trabajadores quedaron reducidos a necrófagos putrefactos y salvajes, condenados a merodear por la tierra en ruinas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Culling the ravenous ghouls at the patch is vital to securing the northern roadway between Silverpine Forest and the safety of Undercity.",["race:Undead"]="The ruined farm stands as a bitter reminder of the Plague of Undeath that tore Lordaeron apart, showing the horrifying mindless fate the Forsaken narrowly escaped."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm was struck down by the Plague of Undeath during the Third War. Farmer Ivar, his family, and his workers all succumbed, rising again as feral, rotting ghouls under the lingering sway of the Scourge.",["al"]={"ivar patch history","who was ivar","what happened to ivar"},["q"]="What happened to the farm and its owner?"},{["a"]="Deathstalkers Rane and Quinn Yorick were part of a scouting reconnaissance squad dispatched to gauge regional threats in Silverpine Forest. While passing through, they were ambushed by the ghouls, and Quinn was severely injured by Ivar the Foul, forcing them to take refuge inside the dilapidated farmhouse.",["al"]={"deathstalkers at ivar patch","why are forsaken here","quinn yorick farmhouse"},["q"]="Why are there Deathstalkers hiding inside the house?"},{["a"]="No. The ghouls roaming the pumpkin fields are mindless Scourge remnants created by the Plague of Undeath. They lack free will and will attack any living travelers or Forsaken on sight.",["al"]={"are these ghouls forsaken","scourge in ivar patch","why are ghouls hostile"},["q"]="Are the ghouls here part of the Forsaken?"},{["a"]="The Ivar Patch lies in northern Silverpine Forest, north of the Dead Field and just south of the road leading toward Malden's Orchard.",["al"]={"ivar patch location","where is ivar patch"},["q"]="Where is the Ivar Patch located?"}},["kw"]={"deathstalkers","ghouls","ivar patch","ivar the foul","pumpkin patch","quinn yorick","rane yorick","silverpine forest"},["n"]="Ivar Patch",["s"]="The Ivar Patch is a blighted pumpkin farm located in northern Silverpine Forest. Once a thriving agricultural homestead of Lordaeron, its residents were wiped out during the Third War and transformed into ravenous, mindlessly hostile ghouls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War swept through Lordaeron, this pumpkin patch was a prosperous homestead owned by a farmer named Ivar, who employed a lively crew of farmhands and servants. When the Scourge unleashed the Plague of Undeath across the countryside, the farm was consumed completely. Rather than rising with their minds intact like the free-willed Forsaken, Ivar, his family, and his laborers were reduced to rotting, feral ghouls bound to prowl the ruined soil.",["t"]="A Ruined Harvest"},{["b"]="When the Forsaken began securing northern Silverpine, three Deathstalkers—Rane Yorick, Quinn Yorick, and Erland McKree—scouted the region to evaluate local threats. Passing through the Dead Field, the patrol was ambushed by the feral pack at the patch. Quinn was badly mauled by Ivar himself, now known as Ivar the Foul. With Quinn gravely wounded, the Yoricks fortified themselves inside the farm's old ruined house while McKree pressed on alone toward Malden's Orchard.",["t"]="The Deathstalker Ambush"}}}}}
t["subzone:jaggedswine-farm"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,287,26.461.0,16.432.0,40.145.0,42.139.0,41.213.0,41.171.0",["h"]="0d4155",["n"]="La Pocilga",["s"]="La Pocilga. La Pocilga es una modesta granja de ganado situada en el norte de Durotar, justo al sur de la entrada principal de Orgrimmar. Compuesta por un cobertizo de almacenamiento de madera, un extenso corral y una charca enfangada, sirve como una fuente de alimento crucial que cría resistentes cerdos para la cercana capital de la Horda. Excavada en la implacable y calcinada tierra de Durotar, La Pocilga representa la dura realidad de mantener una fortaleza urbana como Orgrimmar. La tierra roja de la región ofrece una agricultura escasa, lo que hace que el ganado robusto sea esencial para alimentar a miles de guerreros y trabajadores orcos. La granja se articula en torno a un almacén de madera, un amplio corral de estacas y una charca natural donde se pastorea, cría y sacrifica a los cerdos para mantener abastecidos los graneros de la Horda.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Establishing stable meat supplies in the arid wastes of Durotar is a matter of survival, making outposts like Jaggedswine vital to sustaining Orgrimmar's military strength.",["profession:Cooking"]="For Horde cooks learning their trade in Durotar, the abundant swine around Jaggedswine Farm make it a primary local source for tender ribs, pork cuts, and cooking grease."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The farm raises and maintains swine to provide meat and lard for the Horde, particularly to feed the population and garrison of nearby Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"what is jaggedswine farm","why is there a pig farm in durotar","jaggedswine farm purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of Jaggedswine Farm?"},{["a"]="It lies in northern Durotar, sitting just outside the southern approach and grand gates that lead into the Valley of Strength in Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"where is jaggedswine farm","how to get to jaggedswine farm","pig farm durotar location"},["q"]="Where exactly is Jaggedswine Farm located?"},{["a"]="Orcish livestock farming in Durotar is utilitarian and unglamorous. Between free-roaming boars and sparse timber structures, the steading lacks grand homesteads, but it remains actively used by Horde supply lines.",["al"]={"is jaggedswine farm abandoned","who lives at jaggedswine farm","why no farmers"},["q"]="Why does the farm look somewhat deserted?"},{["a"]="While the domesticated swine inside the pens are docile, wild and mature boars roaming the outskirts can be aggressive if startled by young travelers or careless foragers.",["al"]={"are swine hostile","do pigs attack here","swine dangerous"},["q"]="Are the pigs here dangerous to travelers?"}},["kw"]={"boars","durotar","horde provisions","jaggedswine farm","orgrimmar","pig pen","pigs","swine"},["n"]="Jaggedswine Farm",["s"]="Jaggedswine Farm is a modest livestock steading situated in northern Durotar, just south of the main entrance to Orgrimmar. Comprising a timber storage shed, a sprawling pen, and a muddy watering hole, it serves as a critical food source raising hardy swine for the nearby Horde capital.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Carved out of Durotar's unforgiving, sunbaked earth, Jaggedswine Farm represents the harsh reality of sustaining an urban stronghold like Orgrimmar. The red soil of the region yields sparse agriculture, making robust livestock essential to feeding thousands of orcish warriors and laborers. The farm centers on a timber storehouse, a wide wooden pen, and a natural watering pond where swine are herded, bred, and butchered to keep the Horde's granaries stocked.",["t"]="Provisions for the Capital"},{["b"]="Though quiet and often appearing half-tended under the dry heat, the farm is a regular stomping ground for local swineherds and patrolling Orgrimmar Grunts. Wild and mature swine roam both inside and outside the enclosures, occasionally testing the patience of nearby guards. Sitting right on the threshold of the capital's valley approach, the plot remains an unassuming yet indispensable outpost in the daily logistics of Durotar.",["t"]="A Quiet Frontier"}}}}}
t["subzone:jangolode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,217,20.391.0,27.177.0,32.120.0,40.228.0",["h"]="e1f904",["n"]="Mina de Jango",["s"]="Mina de Jango. La Mina de Jango es una rica excavación minera ubicada en las onduladas colinas de Páramos de Poniente. Antaño una fuente vital de mineral y materias primas para Ciudad de Ventormenta, la mina ha sido tomada por los bandidos de la Hermandad Defias. Antes de que Páramos de Poniente cayera en decadencia, la Mina de Jango proporcionaba un flujo constante de metales cruciales para la reconstrucción y el abastecimiento de Ciudad de Ventormenta. A medida que el orden civil se deterioró y el reino retiró sus guarniciones, la Hermandad Defias se hizo con el control del enclave para abastecer sus propias operaciones. Los bandidos ahora explotan las ricas vetas para sí mismos, defendiendo con fiereza su botín subterráneo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Reclaiming Westfall's resources is vital for stabilizing the kingdom, and driving the bandits out of Jangolode is one step toward restoring the region's prosperity.",["profession:Mining"]="The Jangolode Mine remains rich in basic copper and tin deposits, making it a lucrative stop for prospectors willing to fight past the subterranean pests."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is an excavation site in Westfall that historically supplied Stormwind City with essential minerals and metal ore. With regional defense weakened, it fell into hostile hands.",["al"]={"jangolode mine info","what is jangolode","jangolode westfall"},["q"]="What is the Jangolode Mine?"},{["a"]="The Defias Brotherhood holds the underground shafts, having driven out the original miners to feed their own operations.",["al"]={"who is in jangolode mine","jangolode mobs","who lives in jangolode"},["q"]="Who controls the mine right now?"},{["a"]="Stormwind is mired in political unrest and struggling to protect even its core borders. The kingdom lacks the troops to garrison Westfall's outlying mines, leaving the People's Militia and local adventurers to manage the threat.",["al"]={"why doesnt stormwind clear jangolode","stormwind garrison westfall","why abandon the mine"},["q"]="Why does Stormwind not reclaim the mine?"}},["kw"]={"defias brotherhood","jangolode","jangolode mine","kobold","stormwind","westfall"},["n"]="Jangolode Mine",["s"]="Jangolode Mine is a rich mineral excavation located in the rolling hills of Westfall. Once a vital source of ore and raw materials for Stormwind City, the mine has been seized by the bandits of the Defias Brotherhood.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before Westfall fell into decline, the Jangolode Mine provided a steady flow of metals crucial to the reconstruction and supply of Stormwind City. As civil order deteriorated and the kingdom withdrew its garrisons, the Defias Brotherhood seized control of the site to feed their own operations. The bandits now work the rich veins for themselves, fiercely defending their subterranean prize.",["t"]="A Plundered Resource"}}}}}
t["subzone:jansen-stead"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,287,18.566.0,30.142.0,36.188.0,52.253.0,30.196.0",["h"]="ed83cd",["n"]="La Finca de Jansen",["s"]="La Finca de Jansen. La Finca de Jansen es la granja más septentrional de los Páramos de Poniente, situada siguiendo el camino que sale del puente al Bosque de Elwynn. Al igual que gran parte del granero circundante, la hacienda ha escapado de las manos de los campesinos y está plagada de Vigías de la cosecha mecánicos rebeldes y bandidos de los Defias errantes. Situada justo al cruzar la frontera de Elwynn, La Finca de Jansen representa la dura realidad que recibe a cualquiera que viaje hacia el oeste, rumbo a los Páramos de Poniente. Antaño una próspera granja familiar que abastecía al reino, sus legítimos ocupantes han sido expulsados por la creciente ola de disturbios. En su lugar, hostiles Vigías de la cosecha —autómatas mecánicos defectuosos reprogramados por la Hermandad Defias— patrullan los campos marchitos junto a bandoleros. Su cercanía al camino principal la convierte en un peligro temprano y notable para mensajeros y viajeros que transitan entre Villadorada y Colina del Centinela.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The farmstead's fall underscores the failure of Stormwind's leadership to secure its own borders, leaving defenseless homesteaders at the mercy of outlaws within sight of Elwynn Forest.",["race:Human"]="For humans crossing over from the relative peace of Northshire and Elwynn, the ruin of Jansen Stead offers a harsh awakening to the economic crisis and banditry paralyzing Stormwind's rural heartland."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the very first farmstead on the right-hand side of the road as you cross the river bridge from Elwynn Forest into northeastern Westfall.",["al"]={"jansen stead location","where is jansen stead","jansen farm westfall"},["q"]="Where is Jansen Stead located?"},{["a"]="The farm's original residents have been displaced. Today, the overgrown fields and derelict farmhouse are occupied by hostile Harvest Watchers and footpads loyal to the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"who is at jansen stead","jansen stead inhabitants","mobs at jansen stead"},["q"]="Who lives at Jansen Stead right now?"},{["a"]="The mechanical golems known as Harvest Watchers were originally built to tend crops and harvest wheat. The Defias Brotherhood has commandeered and reprogrammed them into deadly sentries to protect their illicit operations and drive out loyalist farmers.",["al"]={"why harvest watchers attack","mechanical golems westfall","defias scarecrows"},["q"]="Why are mechanical scarecrows attacking people here?"},{["a"]="Just south of the bridge near the entrance to Jansen Stead, Farmer Furlbrow and his wife Verna have set up camp by their broken wagon, having been forced off their own pumpkin patch down the road.",["al"]={"quests near jansen stead","furlbrows location","who gives quests near elwynn bridge"},["q"]="Who is nearby asking for help?"}},["kw"]={"defias","farm","furlbrow","harvest watcher","jansen","stead","westfall"},["n"]="Jansen Stead",["s"]="Jansen Stead is the northernmost farmstead in Westfall, situated just down the road from the bridge to Elwynn Forest. Like much of the surrounding breadbasket, the homestead has fallen out of peasant hands and is swarming with rogue mechanical Harvest Watchers and roving Defias bandits.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned right past the Elwynn border, the Jansen Stead represents the harsh reality greeting anyone traveling westward into Westfall. Once a flourishing family farm feeding the kingdom, its rightful occupants have been driven away by the rising tide of unrest. In their place, hostile Harvest Watchers—malfunctioning clockwork automatons reprogrammed by the Defias Brotherhood—patrol the blighted fields alongside brigands. Its proximity to the main road makes it a prominent early hazard for couriers and travelers moving between Goldshire and Sentinel Hill.",["t"]="A Fallen Homestead"}}}}}
t["subzone:jasperlode-mine"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,272,25.414.0,19.391.0,31.218.0,56.215.0,35.162.0,43.235.0",["h"]="e24fa2",["n"]="Cantera de Jaspe",["s"]="Cantera de Jaspe. La Cantera de Jaspe es una excavación de hierro y minerales situada en la zona centronorte del Bosque de Elwynn que antaño abastecía a Ciudad de Ventormenta con recursos vitales. En la actualidad, los pozos están invadidos por enjambres de kóbolds y letales arañas gigantes, lo que deja al mermado reino sin capacidad para recuperarla. Históricamente, la Cantera de Jaspe fue una de las operaciones mineras más productivas de Ventormenta, proporcionando una constante riqueza mineral junto a la cercana Mina Abisal. Como el ejército del reino apenas da abasto para hacer frente a las amenazas externas y a los disturbios, las guarniciones locales se han visto incapaces de proteger los pozos. Los kóbolds aprovecharon la oportunidad para excavar en su interior, expulsando a los mineros humanos y acumulando oro robado y velas de sebo.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Securing raw metal from Jasperlode is vital to maintaining Stormwind's equipment supplies during a time when the kingdom's borders face constant peril.",["profession:Mining"]="Rich in mineral veins, Jasperlode remains an enticing target for prospectors willing to fight through kobold pickaxes and spider webs to stake a claim."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Stormwind's standing army is spread thin across the realm, leaving rural outposts like Goldshire short on manpower. Opportunistic kobolds quickly swarmed the dig sites once the human miners lost their guard protection.",["al"]={"why are there kobolds","who controls jasperlode","why abandoned"},["q"]="Why is Jasperlode Mine overrun?"},{["a"]="Fargodeep Mine lies to the south near the Maclure and Stonefield farms, while Jasperlode sits to the north nestled in the foothills near the river. Both are major Elwynn mineral sites lost to the kobold infestation.",["al"]={"jasperlode vs fargodeep","other elwynn mine"},["q"]="What is the difference between Jasperlode and Fargodeep?"},{["a"]="The deepest shafts are infested with predatory mine spiders led by a massive arachnid known as Mother Fang. Even the occupying kobolds avoid their webbed caverns.",["al"]={"spiders in jasperlode","mother fang","what is at the bottom"},["q"]="What lurks in the back of the mine?"},{["a"]="Marshal Dughan lacks the troops to mount a prolonged subterranean clearing. Between Defias river patrols, gnoll incursions, and garrison duties, the local militia must rely on traveling adventurers to scout and cull the threats inside.",["al"]={"why no stormwind guard","dughan sending soldiers"},["q"]="Why hasn't Marshal Dughan cleared the mine?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","fargodeep","gold dust","goldshire","jasperlode","kobold","marshal dughan","mother fang"},["n"]="Jasperlode Mine",["s"]="Jasperlode Mine is an iron and mineral excavation in north-central Elwynn Forest that once supplied Stormwind City with vital resources. Today, the shafts are overrun by swarming kobolds and deadly giant spiders, leaving the resource-strapped kingdom unable to reclaim it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Jasperlode Mine was historically one of Stormwind's most productive mining operations, providing steady mineral wealth alongside nearby Fargodeep. With the kingdom's military stretched thin defending against external threats and unrest, local garrisons have been unable to protect the shafts. Kobolds seized the opportunity to burrow inside, driving human miners out and stockpiling stolen gold and tallow candles.",["t"]="A Lost Resource in Elwynn"},{["b"]="The infestation within Jasperlode extends beyond simple vermin. In the deepest, darkest corridors beneath the timber supports, an aggressive colony of mine spiders has taken root. Led by a massive matriarch known to locals as Mother Fang, the spiders treat trespassing kobolds—and any unwary prospectors—as effortless prey, making any attempt to salvage the mine exceptionally hazardous.",["t"]="Dangers in the Deep"}}}}}
t["subzone:jerod-s-landing"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,255,21.490.0,19.384.1,33.175.0,29.163.0,48.194.0,42.163.0",["h"]="7e3a35",["n"]="Embarcadero de Jerod",["s"]="Embarcadero de Jerod. El Embarcadero de Jerod es un modesto muelle fluvial situado en la orilla del río Nazferiti correspondiente al Bosque de Elwynn. Actualmente tomado por la Hermandad Defias, este puesto de avanzada sirve como punto de transferencia clandestino para cargamentos ilícitos que se introducen de contrabando a través de las vías fluviales del reino. Escondido a lo largo de las aguas orientales del río Nazferiti, el Embarcadero de Jerod proporciona acceso fluvial que conecta el Bosque de Elwynn con los territorios vecinos. Aunque en su origen era un simple muelle para botes, el lugar ha caído firmemente en manos de la Hermandad Defias. Bajo la atenta mirada de un maestro de dársena Defias, los forajidos utilizan el muelle como centro para recibir mercancías saqueadas en las Montañas Crestagrana, trasladando discretamente los cargamentos río abajo hacia posesiones como La torre de Klaven en los Páramos de Poniente.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="Rogues working on behalf of SI:7 are dispatched to Jerod's Landing to test their stealth, pickpocket the Defias dockmaster, and recover sensitive trade ledgers.",["faction:Alliance"]="The occupation of Jerod's Landing highlights how thoroughly the Defias have compromised the interior waterways linking Elwynn to Redridge right beneath Stormwind's nose."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Jerod's Landing is located in eastern Elwynn Forest, resting along the western bank of the Nazferiti River, which marks the boundary between Elwynn and the Redridge Mountains.",["al"]={"jerods landing location","where is jerod's landing","jerod dock map"},["q"]="Where is Jerod's Landing located?"},{["a"]="The landing has been occupied by members of the Defias Brotherhood, led by a Defias dockmaster who coordinates shipments with armed bandits guarding the waterside.",["al"]={"who is at jerods landing","defias at jerods landing","jerod landing mobs"},["q"]="Who controls Jerod's Landing?"},{["a"]="The Brotherhood utilizes the dock as a smuggling waystation to transport stolen goods and weaponry intercepted in the Redridge Mountains toward rogue strongholds like Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",["al"]={"why do defias use jerods landing","defias river smuggling"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this dock for the Defias?"},{["a"]="Master Mathias Shaw and his intelligence agents track the flow of Defias contraband through this dock to expose the network linking Westfall, Elwynn, and Redridge.",["al"]={"si7 jerods landing","rogue quest jerods landing"},["q"]="Why is SI:7 interested in Jerod's Landing?"}},["kw"]={"defias dockmaster","jerod's landing","klaven's tower","mathias shaw","nazferiti river","smuggling","snatch and grab"},["n"]="Jerod's Landing",["s"]="Jerod's Landing is a modest river dock situated on the Elwynn Forest bank of the Nazferiti River. Currently seized by the Defias Brotherhood, the outpost serves as a clandestine transfer point for illicit shipments smuggled across the kingdom's waterways.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away along the eastern waters of the Nazferiti River, Jerod's Landing provides river access connecting Elwynn Forest to neighboring territories. While originally an ordinary boat dock, the site has fallen firmly into the hands of the Defias Brotherhood. Under the watchful eye of a Defias dockmaster, outlaws utilize the dock as a hub to receive goods plundered from the Redridge Mountains, discreetly moving river cargo downstream toward holdings such as Klaven's Tower in Westfall.",["t"]="A Smuggler's Waypoint"},{["b"]="Because of its strategic placement on the river, Jerod's Landing has drawn the attention of SI:7, Stormwind's covert intelligence network. Operatives monitoring Defias operations view the landing as a vital link in the syndicate's supply lines, sending resourceful rogues to infiltrate the docks, pilfer river shipment ledgers, and unravel the wider conspiracy strangling the kingdom.",["t"]="Eyes in the Shadows"}}}}}
t["subzone:kargathia-keep"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,261,26.521.0,22.373.0,32.129.0,19.158.0,33.195.0,49.185.0",["h"]="bd1bb9",["n"]="Fuerte de Kargathia",["s"]="Fuerte de Kargathia. El Fuerte de Kargathia es un bastión fortificado de la Horda que afianza el frente oriental del Aserradero Grito de Guerra en Vallefresno. Al servir como cuartel general de los capataces del puesto de avanzada, vigila la frontera fluvial y garantiza líneas de refuerzo rápido directas a Orgrimmar. Encaramado en el extremo oriental del Aserradero Grito de Guerra, justo al oeste del Río Furia del Sur, el Fuerte de Kargathia sirve como Centro de Mando para las operaciones madereras de la Horda en Vallefresno. Mejorado con pesadas barricadas de púas, este puesto fortificado alberga al Capataz Gorthak y a sus oficiales. Su posición estratégica junto a la frontera fluvial permite al clan Grito de Guerra vigilar las incursiones que se aproximan y recibir refuerzos rápidos directamente desde las tierras vecinas de Durotar y Orgrimmar siempre que atacan las escaramuzas de los elfos de la noche.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="For Horde defenders, Kargathia Keep is an indispensable sanctuary on the frontline of Ashenvale, securing valuable timber shipments vital to Orgrimmar's construction.",["race:NightElf"]="To the night elves, this heavily spiked stronghold represents the aggressive, deeply entrenched nature of the Horde's intrusion into their sacred ancestral forest."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kargathia Keep is situated in eastern Ashenvale, on the eastern edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp just west of the Southfury River.",["al"]={"kargathia keep location","where is kargathia keep","kargathia outpost location"},["q"]="Where is Kargathia Keep located?"},{["a"]="Overseer Gorthak commands the Warsong Lumber Camp from within Kargathia Keep, directing logging operations and coordinating defenses against Alliance attacks.",["al"]={"who is in charge of kargathia keep","kargathia keep leader","overseer gorthak"},["q"]="Who leads the keep?"},{["a"]="The stronghold was named in honor of Kargath Bladefist, the legendary chieftain of the Shattered Hand clan, sharing this naming heritage with Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay in Durotar.",["al"]={"who is kargathia keep named after","kargath bladefist","why kargathia"},["q"]="Why was the keep named Kargathia?"},{["a"]="The keep commands the eastern border of the logging camp along the Southfury River, securing the vital supply route and enabling rapid troop reinforcements to cross over from Orgrimmar.",["al"]={"why is kargathia keep here","purpose of kargathia keep","kargathia keep importance"},["q"]="What is the strategic purpose of this stronghold?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","kargath bladefist","kargathia keep","kargathia outpost","overseer gorthak","southfury river","warsong lumber camp"},["n"]="Kargathia Keep",["s"]="Kargathia Keep is a fortified Horde stronghold anchoring the eastern front of the Warsong Lumber Camp in Ashenvale. Serving as headquarters for the outpost's overseers, it guards the river border and ensures rapid reinforcement lines directly back to Orgrimmar.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the eastern edge of the Warsong Lumber Camp just west of the Southfury River, Kargathia Keep serves as the command center for the Horde's logging operations in Ashenvale. Upgraded with heavy spiked barricades, this fortified outpost houses Overseer Gorthak and his officers. Its strategic position against the river border allows the Warsong clan to monitor incoming incursions and receive swift reinforcements directly from the neighboring lands of Durotar and Orgrimmar whenever night elf skirmishers strike.",["t"]="A Bastion on the Southfury"},{["b"]="Like the fortress of Kargath in the Badlands and Bladefist Bay along the coast of Durotar, the outpost takes its name from the famed chieftain Kargath Bladefist. For the Warsong orcs braving Ashenvale's hostile woodlands, the keep's imposing classic architecture stands as an enduring symbol of martial resilience and Horde defiance in territory claimed by the night elves.",["t"]="Honoring the Bladefist"}}}}}
t["subzone:kharanos"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="8,268,23.544.0,21.508.0,17.221.0,45.237.0,31.190.0,26.173.0",["h"]="0bec10",["n"]="Kharanos",["s"]="Kharanos. Kharanos es un bullicioso asentamiento montañoso situado en el corazón nevado de Dun Morogh, siguiendo el camino desde Forjaz. Como centro neurálgico principal para los viajeros que parten de Valle de Crestanevada, la localidad alberga una forja, talleres gnómicos y la célebre Destilería Cebatruenos. Ubicado a lo largo del camino central de Dun Morogh, Kharanos es el primer pueblo propiamente dicho que da la bienvenida a los reclutas que llegan de Yunquemar. Pese al gélido frío y a los vientos cortantes, el asentamiento prospera gracias al coraje de los enanos locales y al ingenio gnómico. Su vida gira en torno a una ardiente forja pública y a la Destilería Cebatruenos, famosa en las montañas orientales por elaborar una de las mejores cervezas de Khaz Modan. Entre artesanos atareados y fatigados viajeros en busca de abrigo, la población se erige en el punto neurálgico indispensable para los asuntos de los picos inferiores.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Dwarf"]="For dwarves leaving the sheltered crags of Coldridge Pass, Kharanos is the first taste of the wider kingdom, filled with steaming forges and the legendary stout of the Thunderbrew clan.",["race:Gnome"]="Refugees and tinkerers from Gnomeregan frequently base themselves in and around Kharanos, collaborating with local smiths and operating out of nearby depots."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kharanos is the primary dwarf and gnome settlement in central Dun Morogh. It acts as a crossroads connecting Coldridge Valley, Ironforge, and the outer wilderness, featuring essential trade, training services, and an inn.",["al"]={"kharanos overview","where is kharanos","kharanos town"},["q"]="What is Kharanos?"},{["a"]="The town features the famous Thunderbrew Distillery, which serves as an inn and taproom, as well as a large public forge and class and profession trainers. Nearby workshops like Steelgrill's Depot provide mechanized engineering supplies.",["al"]={"kharanos trainers","what is in kharanos","kharanos inn"},["q"]="What services and facilities are in Kharanos?"},{["a"]="Kharanos faces constant pressure from aggressive Frostmane troll tribes entrenched on Shimmer Ridge to the northwest, as well as predatory wendigo roaming the icy caves directly to the west.",["al"]={"kharanos enemies","frostmane trolls kharanos","wendigo kharanos"},["q"]="What threats endanger the town?"},{["a"]="Lazlo Grindwidget is remembered as a local folk hero who saved Kharanos when a massive Frostmane troll assaulted the settlement and nearly overwhelmed the dwarven defenders.",["al"]={"lazlo hero","who saved kharanos","giant troll attack kharanos"},["q"]="Who was Lazlo Grindwidget?"}},["kw"]={"distillery","dun morogh","frostmane","kharanos","lazlo grindwidget","shimmer ridge","thunderbrew"},["n"]="Kharanos",["s"]="Kharanos is a bustling mountain settlement nestled in the snowy heart of Dun Morogh, just down the road from Ironforge. Serving as the primary hub for travelers leaving Coldridge Valley, the town hosts a forge, gnomish workshops, and the famous Thunderbrew Distillery.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated along the central road of Dun Morogh, Kharanos is the first true town welcoming recruits arriving from Anvilmar. Despite the biting cold and biting winds, the settlement thrives thanks to local dwarven grit and gnomish ingenuity. It centers around a roaring public forge and the Thunderbrew Distillery, renowned across the eastern mountains for producing some of the finest ale in Khaz Modan. Between bustling crafters and weary travelers seeking warmth, the town stands as the essential staging ground for business in the lower peaks.",["t"]="A Hearty Frontier Haven"},{["b"]="Behind its cozy hearths, Kharanos serves as a vital military outpost tasked with keeping the mountain passes secure. Fierce indigenous wendigo prowl the frozen caverns directly to the west, while aggressive Frostmane trolls remain entrenched atop Shimmer Ridge to the northwest. With Ironforge's regular forces stretched thin across the realm, the town relies heavily on visiting adventurers and local watchmen to drive back raiding parties, cull dangerous predators, and ensure the trade routes remain open.",["t"]="Guarding the Lowlands"}}}}}
t["subzone:kodo-rock"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,395,22.444.0,22.386.0,27.206.0,30.240.0,45.214.0,32.197.0",["h"]="0f93b2",["n"]="Roca de los Kodos",["s"]="Roca de los Kodos. La Roca de los Kodos es un monumento de piedra natural situado en las llanuras de la Mesa de la Nube Roja, entre el Campamento Narache y el Barranco Cortazarza. Alzándose en silencio entre las hierbas de Mulgore, sirve como un temprano lugar de peregrinación para los jóvenes chamanes tauren que aprenden a comunicarse con los espíritus de la tierra. Debido a su modesta silueta frente al ondulado paisaje, los viajeros deben afinar la vista para avistarla. Situada aproximadamente a mitad de camino por el sendero que conecta el Campamento Narache con el hostil territorio jabaespín del Barranco Cortazarza, la Roca de los Kodos se distingue por una parcela de tierra desgastada en su base. Aunque carece de la imponente grandeza de los elevados riscos que rodean la Mesa de la Nube Roja, su perfil característico recuerda a las veneradas bestias kodo que recorren las praderas. Para los miembros de las tribus errantes, actúa como una apacible baliza natural en las ventosas llanuras de Mulgore.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Shaman"]="For novice tauren shamans beginning their spiritual path at Camp Narache, Kodo Rock is a vital landmark used to attune with the elemental world.",["race:Tauren"]="The stone formation serves as a familiar landmark across the plains of Red Cloud Mesa, reflecting the sacred bond between the Shu'halo and the beasts of Mulgore."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kodo Rock is situated on Red Cloud Mesa in Mulgore. You can find it roughly halfway along a straight path between Camp Narache and Brambleblade Ravine, marked on the ground by a small clearing of bare dirt.",["al"]={"kodo rock location","where is kodo rock","find kodo rock"},["q"]="Where is Kodo Rock located?"},{["a"]="The monument blends naturally into the rolling hills and grasses of the mesa. It is only clearly visible from a relatively short distance, requiring travelers to pay close attention to the terrain and watch for the patch of dirt beneath it.",["al"]={"cant find kodo rock","kodo rock hidden"},["q"]="Why is Kodo Rock hard to find?"},{["a"]="Tauren shamans visit the rock during their earliest trials out of Camp Narache. It serves as a peaceful, sacred landmark for novices learning to attune their spirits to the land and the elemental forces of Mulgore.",["al"]={"shaman quest kodo rock","why go to kodo rock"},["q"]="Why is Kodo Rock important to tauren shamans?"},{["a"]="While the immediate patch around Kodo Rock is generally peaceful, heading further northeast leads directly toward Brambleblade Ravine, a canyon densely populated by aggressive Bristleback quilboar.",["al"]={"is kodo rock safe","enemies near kodo rock"},["q"]="What dangers are near Kodo Rock?"}},["kw"]={"brambleblade ravine","camp narache","kodo rock","monument","mulgore","red cloud mesa","shaman trial","tauren shaman"},["n"]="Kodo Rock",["s"]="Kodo Rock is a natural stone monument located in the plains of Red Cloud Mesa, between Camp Narache and Brambleblade Ravine. Standing quietly amid the grasses of Mulgore, it serves as an early pilgrimage site for young tauren shamans learning to commune with the spirits of the earth. Because of its modest silhouette against the rolling landscape, travelers must keep a keen eye out to spot it.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated roughly halfway along the path connecting Camp Narache to the hostile quillboar territory of Brambleblade Ravine, Kodo Rock is marked by a patch of worn earth at its base. While it lacks the sheer grandeur of the towering bluffs surrounding Red Cloud Mesa, its distinct profile resembles the revered kodo beasts that wander the grasslands. For wandering tribesfolk, it acts as a quiet natural beacon in the windswept plains of Mulgore.",["t"]="A Waypoint on the Mesa"},{["b"]="To the Shu'halo, natural formations often carry spiritual weight. Kodo Rock holds special reverence for young tauren shamans beginning their spiritual walk. Novices are directed here on early rites of passage, using the solitary stone monument as a sacred grounds to commune with elemental forces and honor the natural world before venturing into more perilous reaches of the continent.",["t"]="Spiritual Significance"}}}}}
t["subzone:kolkar-crag"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,219,25.544.0,19.461.1,25.181.0,45.217.0,27.170.0",["h"]="ec887c",["n"]="Risco Kolkar",["s"]="Risco Kolkar. Risco Kolkar es un desfiladero escarpado y abrasado por el sol situado en el sur de Durotar, reclamado por los hostiles centauros Kolkar. Liderado por el señor de la guerra Kolkanis, este enclave sirve como base de operaciones para incursiones coordinadas contra los asentamientos cercanos de la Horda. Oculto entre los abruptos cañones del sur de Durotar, Risco Kolkar es una base de operaciones para el agresivo clan Kolkar. A pesar del terreno árido e implacable, estos centauros han fortificado los pasos estrechos naturales del desfiladero. Desde este barranco, sus exploradores y merodeadores vigilan de cerca las llanuras circundantes, buscando puntos débiles en las posesiones de los orcos y los Lanza Negra. Para los jóvenes guerreros que entrenan en el Valle de los Retos o patrullan la costa sur, Risco Kolkar representa el frente organizado de hostilidad de los centauros más cercano.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Securing southern Durotar against centaur incursions protects the supply lines running between Sen'jin Village and the road to Orgrimmar.",["race:Orc"]="The presence of centaur so close to the Valley of Trials threatens the initiation of young orcs, making the pacification of Kolkar Crag an urgent matter of territorial defense."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Kolkar Crag is held by the Kolkar centaur clan, led on-site by Warlord Kolkanis. They use the defensible canyon as a camp and raiding post against Horde outposts throughout Durotar.",["al"]={"who is at kolkar crag","kolkar crag inhabitants","who owns kolkar crag"},["q"]="Who lives in Kolkar Crag?"},{["a"]="The centaur within the gorge have drafted plans to launch coordinated assaults on Durotar's vital settlements, including the training grounds in the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and Orgrimmar itself.",["al"]={"why care about kolkar crag","is kolkar crag dangerous","kolkar threat"},["q"]="Why is the Horde concerned about this ravine?"},{["a"]="The encampment is commanded by Warlord Kolkanis, a ferocious centaur warlord who directs their scouting maneuvers and formulates battle plans against the orcs and trolls.",["al"]={"kolkar crag boss","who leads kolkar crag","warlord kolkanis"},["q"]="Who leads the centaur here?"}},["kw"]={"centaur","durotar","kolkanis","kolkar","kolkar crag","sen'jin village","valley of trials","warlord kolkanis"},["n"]="Kolkar Crag",["s"]="Kolkar Crag is a sunbaked, jagged gorge in southern Durotar claimed by the hostile Kolkar centaur. Led by Warlord Kolkanis, this enclave serves as a staging ground for coordinated raids against nearby Horde settlements.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away in the rugged canyons of southern Durotar, Kolkar Crag is a base of operations for the aggressive Kolkar clan. Despite the arid and unforgiving terrain, these centaur have fortified the natural choke points of the gorge. From this ravine, their scouts and marauders keep close watch over the surrounding flats, probing for vulnerabilities across orc and Darkspear holdings. For young warriors training in the Valley of Trials or patrolling the southern coast, Kolkar Crag represents the nearest organized front of centaur hostility.",["t"]="A Thorn in Durotar's Side"},{["b"]="Under the command of Warlord Kolkanis, the centaur entrenched at the crag hold ambitions far beyond simple skirmishes. Recovered attack plans reveal plots targeting the Valley of Trials, Sen'jin Village, Razor Hill, and daring strikes aimed directly toward the gates of Orgrimmar. Halting these plans requires decisive preemptive strikes deep into the ravine to assassinate Kolkanis and break their muster before their war parties can sweep through the valleys.",["t"]="Schemes of Invasion"}}}}}
t["subzone:lake-al-ameth"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,291,20.551.0,18.386.0,31.96.0,51.198.0,45.136.0,18.173.0",["h"]="87b28f",["n"]="Lago Al'Ameth",["s"]="Lago Al'Ameth. El Lago Al'Ameth es una de las mayores masas de agua dulce situadas en lo alto de las ramas de Teldrassil, justo al sur de Dolanaar. Aunque antaño fue un remanso de paz que apenas contaba con un sencillo embarcadero de madera, sus orillas se han vuelto peligrosas debido a la violenta agitación de la vegetación local. Situado inmediatamente al sur de la aldea de Dolanaar, el Lago Al'Ameth actúa como una cuenca natural vital en el corazón de Teldrassil. A pesar de sus aguas serenas y sus escasos asentamientos, la paz aquí se ha esfumado. Enjambres de brezomaderas agitados y Brotes de Brezomadera merodean por la orilla, enloquecidos por una enfermedad antinatural que se propaga por el Árbol del Mundo. Los druidas e investigadores de Dolanaar envían con frecuencia a viajeros a estas orillas para recoger semillas y abatir a las agresivas criaturas antes de que la corrupción penetre más profundamente en el bosque circundante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="The wild timberlings around the lake offer druids a hands-on study of the unnatural corruption undermining Teldrassil's flora and fauna.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth is an alarming sign of the ailments troubling their newly raised home, forcing young defenders to protect the surrounding road."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lake Al'Ameth lies directly south of the night elf settlement of Dolanaar in eastern Teldrassil.",["al"]={"lake alameth location","where is lake al'ameth","find lake al'ameth"},["q"]="Where is Lake Al'Ameth located?"},{["a"]="The timberlings and plant life along the shores have fallen victim to a corrupting sickness afflicting Teldrassil, driving previously harmless woodland spriggans and treants into a territorial rage.",["al"]={"why timberlings angry","lake alameth enemies","aggressive timberlings"},["q"]="Why are the creatures around Lake Al'Ameth hostile?"},{["a"]="The lake is largely wild and undeveloped, featuring only a simple wooden fishing jetty on its northern bank near the path from Dolanaar.",["al"]={"lake alameth pier","dock at lake alameth"},["q"]="What structures or landmarks are on the lake?"},{["a"]="Oakenscowl is a powerful, corrupted ancient lurking near the groves of Lake Al'Ameth. He serves as an embodiment of the violent rot warping the forest creatures in the area.",["al"]={"what is oakenscowl","oakenscowl lake al'ameth"},["q"]="Who is Oakenscowl?"}},["kw"]={"dolanaar","kaldorei","lake al'ameth","oakenscowl","teldrassil","timberling","timberling seeds"},["n"]="Lake Al'Ameth",["s"]="Lake Al'Ameth is one of the largest freshwater bodies nestled high in the boughs of Teldrassil, located just south of Dolanaar. Though once a tranquil haven featuring little more than a simple wooden jetty, its shores have grown perilous due to the violent agitation of the local plant life.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Resting immediately south of the village of Dolanaar, Lake Al'Ameth serves as a vital natural basin in the heart of Teldrassil. Despite its serene waters and minimal settlement, peace here has evaporated. Swarms of agitated timberlings and timberling sprouts prowl the water's edge, driven mad by an unnatural sickness spreading through the world tree. Druids and researchers from Dolanaar frequently dispatch travelers to these shores to gather seeds and cull the aggressive creatures before the corruption spreads deeper into the surrounding forest.",["t"]="A Troubled Shoreline"},{["b"]="The hostility around Lake Al'Ameth is directly tied to the woodland spirits losing their balance. Massive, corrupted treants like Oakenscowl lurk in the nearby groves, while natural timberlings lash out at any who approach. For the Cenarion Circle, diagnosing and treating the rot around Lake Al'Ameth is an urgent test of whether Teldrassil's unblessed creation can truly be sustained.",["t"]="The Roots of Wrath"}}}}}
t["subzone:lake-everstill"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,307,19.444.0,21.502.0,48.215.0,37.249.0,46.123.0,38.212.0",["h"]="d92281",["n"]="Lago Sempiterno",["s"]="Lago Sempiterno. El Lago Sempiterno es la vasta masa de agua azulada que domina el corazón de las Montañas Crestagrana, flanqueando la villa de Villa del Lago. Famoso en el pasado por su pesca tranquila y sus limpias aguas de deshielo montañoso, sus orillas y aguas se han vuelto peligrosas en los últimos tiempos debido a agresivas tribus de múrlocs y bestias lacustres depredadoras. Abarcando la cuenca central de Crestagrana, el Lago Sempiterno conforma el paisaje panorámico y la vía fluvial vital para la villa de Villa del Lago. Sus aguas cristalinas fluyen hacia el este rumbo a las imponentes alturas de Petravista. Cruzado por el puente central del pueblo, el lago ha sustentado durante mucho tiempo el comercio local y a pescadores apacibles, aunque cualquiera que camine hoy por su orilla encontrará que su reputación de sosiego ha sido hecha añicos por las amenazas de la naturaleza circundante.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The lake serves as a cautionary tale in arcane academy texts on portal hygiene, following the disaster in 24 ADP where an unfiltered underwater gateway simultaneously flooded Ironforge and desiccated Lakeshire.",["faction:Alliance"]="Controlling the lake and its crossings is vital for Lakeshire's survival against the coordinated incursions of Redridge murlocs and nearby Blackrock orcs."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shallows are crawling with hostile murloc tribes, including scouts, tidecallers, and flesheaters. Swimming deeper poses its own hazards, as giant threshers and aggressive muckdwellers patrol beneath the surface.",["al"]={"what is in the lake","lake everstill monsters","redridge lake mobs"},["q"]="What dangerous creatures live in Lake Everstill?"},{["a"]="In 24 ADP, a reckless mage opened an unfiltered portal between the lakebed and the mountain city of Ironforge. A massive deluge surged into the dwarven capital, nearly draining Lake Everstill dry in what locals recall as the Great Lakeshire Drought.",["al"]={"lake everstill portal","ironforge flood","lake drained"},["q"]="What was the Great Lakeshire Drought?"},{["a"]="The lake is drained by an eastern river that flows out past the slopes beneath the Blackrock-held stronghold of Stonewatch.",["al"]={"lake everstill river","where does the lake go"},["q"]="Where does the water from Lake Everstill flow?"},{["a"]="While the waters teem with catfish and sagefish, fishing has become extremely dangerous. Murloc raiding parties camp right along the water's edge, and large threshers attack anyone straying too far into the deep.",["al"]={"fishing lake everstill","is it safe to fish lakeshire"},["q"]="Can you fish safely in Lake Everstill?"}},["kw"]={"everstill bridge","ironforge flood","lake everstill","lakeshire","murlocs","ol gummers","redridge"},["n"]="Lake Everstill",["s"]="Lake Everstill is the expansive azure body of water dominating the heart of the Redridge Mountains, flanking the town of Lakeshire. Once celebrated for tranquil fishing and clean mountain runoff, its shores and waters have lately turned treacherous due to aggressive murloc tribes and predatory lake beasts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Spanning the central basin of Redridge, Lake Everstill provides the scenic backdrop and vital waterway for the township of Lakeshire. Its crystal-clear waters drain eastward toward the looming heights of Stonewatch. Spanned by the town's central bridge, the lake has long sustained local trade and quiet anglers, though anyone walking the shoreline today will find its peaceful reputation thoroughly shattered by encroaching wilderness threats.",["t"]="Heart of the Valley"},{["b"]="In recent times, hostile murlocs have established camps along the northern and eastern shallows, disrupting trade and harrying fishermen. Below the surface, aquatic hazards lurk as well, including dangerous threshers that patrol the deeper waters. Adding to the town's grievances, an errant mage accidentally tore open an unfiltered portal beneath the lake just a year ago in 24 ADP, momentarily draining water into Ironforge and sparking both the Great Lakeshire Drought and the Great Ironforge Flood.",["t"]="Trouble in the Depths"}}}}}
t["subzone:lake-falathim"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,369,19.413.0,27.352.0,31.125.0,48.215.0,32.146.0,16.163.0",["h"]="f379a8",["n"]="Lago Falathim",["s"]="Lago Falathim. El Lago Falathim es una tranquila masa de agua ubicada en las boscosas colinas del oeste de Vallefresno, al suroeste de la Atalaya de Maestra. Venerado por el constante roce de la luz de la luna de Elune sobre su superficie tanto de día como de noche, antaño fue un apreciado retiro para los elfos de la noche. En los últimos tiempos, sin embargo, agresivos múrlocs han invadido sus orillas, transformando un refugio sagrado en un peligro constante. Escondido al sureste de La Ensenada de Zoram, el Lago Falathim fue apreciado durante mucho tiempo por los Kaldorei como un santuario pacífico para nadar y pescar. Según las leyendas locales, el suave resplandor de Elune descansa sobre estas aguas a todas horas, sea de día o de noche. A pesar de esta sagrada bendición, feroces múrlocs han avanzado tierra adentro para apoderarse de las costas, anidando en gran número y ahuyentando tanto a viajeros locales como a eruditos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Alliance scouts out of Maestra's Post keep a watchful eye toward Lake Falathim, wary of murloc incursions and seeking word on lost scholars like Teronis.",["race:NightElf"]="For the Kaldorei, Lake Falathim is a reminder of wilderness sanctity under siege, where an idyllic lake touched by Elune's constant moonlight is desecrated by savage murloc tribes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lake Falathim lies in western Ashenvale, tucked into the hills southwest of Maestra's Post and southeast of the Zoram Strand.",["al"]={"lake falathim location","where is lake falathim","find lake falathim"},["q"]="Where is Lake Falathim located?"},{["a"]="The lake holds spiritual significance because the goddess Elune's moonlight is said to perpetually touch its waters, whether by day or by night. Historically, night elves visited its peaceful banks to fish and swim.",["al"]={"why is lake falathim important","lake falathim lore","moonlight lake ashenvale"},["q"]="Why is Lake Falathim special to the night elves?"},{["a"]="The lake has been infested by hostile murlocs that have migrated up from the nearby coastal regions, making the shoreline dangerous for travelers.",["al"]={"lake falathim mobs","what is at lake falathim","lake falathim monsters"},["q"]="What creatures inhabit the lake?"},{["a"]="Teronis was a night elf scholar who ventured out near Lake Falathim and went missing, with his disappearance attributed to the vicious murlocs inhabiting the area.",["al"]={"teronis lake falathim","who is teronis","missing scholar lake falathim"},["q"]="Who was Teronis?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","elune","falathim","lake falathim","maestra's post","moonlight","murloc","teronis"},["n"]="Lake Falathim",["s"]="Lake Falathim is a tranquil body of water nestled in the forested hills of western Ashenvale, southwest of Maestra's Post. Revered for the constant touch of Elune's moonlight upon its surface day and night, it was once a beloved retreat for night elves. In recent days, however, aggressive murlocs have overrun its shores, turning a sacred haven into a perilous hazard.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away southeast of the Zoram Strand, Lake Falathim was long cherished by the Kaldorei as a peaceful sanctuary for swimming and fishing. According to local lore, the gentle radiance of Elune rests upon these waters at all hours, day or night. Despite this sacred blessing, ferocious murlocs have surged inland to seize the shores, nesting in thick numbers and driving away local travelers and scholars alike.",["t"]="Bathed in Moonlight"},{["b"]="The sudden occupation by murlocs has made the lake deadly to solitary wanderers. The night elf scholar Teronis was recently lost somewhere near the water's edge on a mission of inquiry. Given the savage hostility of the amphibians lurking on the banks and in the shallows, the Sentinels fear the worst for any who venture toward the moonlit pool alone.",["t"]="The Scholar's Disappearance"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeridge-highway"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,320,15.451.0,17.420.0,38.189.0,29.249.0,35.187.0,33.181.0",["h"]="e19565",["n"]="Camino del Lago",["s"]="Camino del Lago. El Camino del Lago es una antigua vía que discurre a lo largo de la orilla sur del Lago Sempiterno, en las Montañas Crestagrana. Antaño una arteria vital y muy transitada antes de la Primera Guerra, ha caído en la ruina y el desuso. En la actualidad, manadas errantes de gnolls y orcos Roca Negra hacen que transitar por el camino sea peligroso para los viajeros. Antes de la devastación de la Primera Guerra, el Camino del Lago servía como un bullicioso corredor comercial a través de Crestagrana, transportando mercancías y gentes por la orilla sur del Lago Sempiterno. En aquellos días de paz, los viajeros podían desplazarse entre los asentamientos del valle y las colinas orientales bajo la protección del Reino de Ventormenta. Esa seguridad se hizo añicos cuando la Horda marchó por la región, dejando el este de Crestagrana disputado y desolado.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The highway is a visible reminder of Stormwind's neglected frontiers, where local roads just outside Lakeshire have been surrendered to gnolls and orcs due to a lack of reinforcements."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The road tracks along the southern edge of Lake Everstill, heading eastward out of the Lakeshire area toward the foothills surrounding Stonewatch Keep and the eastern mountains of Redridge.",["al"]={"where does lakeridge highway go","lakeridge highway path","where is lakeridge highway"},["q"]="Where does the Lakeridge Highway lead?"},{["a"]="The highway fell into disuse after the First War, particularly when Blackrock orcs fortified Stonewatch Keep. Without the manpower to secure the road, Stormwind could not maintain it, allowing hostile gnolls to move in and choke off civilian travel.",["al"]={"why is it abandoned","why is lakeridge highway empty","lakeridge highway fallen into disuse"},["q"]="Why is the highway abandoned?"},{["a"]="The highway is primarily haunted by aggressive gnolls that ambush anyone wandering away from Lakeshire, as well as lingering Blackrock orc scouts operating out of the eastern strongholds.",["al"]={"dangers on lakeridge highway","mobs on lakeridge highway","who controls lakeridge highway"},["q"]="What threats wander the road today?"},{["a"]="No. In the peaceful era before the First War, the Lakeridge Highway was a well-maintained, highly traveled route that safely connected the heart of Redridge to its eastern outposts.",["al"]={"lakeridge highway history","highway before the war"},["q"]="Was the highway always dangerous?"}},["kw"]={"gnolls","highway","lake everstill","lakeridge","redridge","road","stonewatch"},["n"]="Lakeridge Highway",["s"]="Lakeridge Highway is an old thoroughfare running along the southern shore of Lake Everstill in the Redridge Mountains. Once a vital and heavily traveled artery prior to the First War, it has fallen into ruin and disuse. Today, roving packs of gnolls and Blackrock orcs make passage along the road perilous for travelers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the devastation of the First War, the Lakeridge Highway served as a bustling trade corridor through Redridge, carrying goods and folk along the southern banks of Lake Everstill. In those peaceful days, travelers could journey between the valley settlements and the eastern heights under the protection of the Kingdom of Stormwind. That safety shattered when the Horde marched through the region, leaving eastern Redridge contested and desolate.",["t"]="A Fallen Artery"},{["b"]="Following the seizure of Stonewatch Keep by Blackrock orcs, regular maintenance and patrols along the highway ceased entirely. The road quickly deteriorated into an overgrown track contested by savage gnoll packs. With Stormwind's military spread thin and unable to reinforce Lakeshire, the highway remains officially unsafe. Any traveler seeking to reach the eastern ridges must now carve a path through gnoll ambushes.",["t"]="Peril on the Road"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeshire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,330,18.631.0,22.599.1,22.196.0,52.283.1,38.230.0,41.243.0",["h"]="ff4915",["n"]="Villa del Lago",["s"]="Villa del Lago. Villa del Lago es el principal asentamiento humano de las Montañas Crestagrana, situado en la orilla norte del Lago Sempiterno. Dirigida por el Magistrado Salomón y protegida por el Alguacil Marris, esta pintoresca villa se encuentra actualmente al borde del colapso debido a los incesantes ataques de los orcos Roca Negra, agresivas manadas de gnolls y los múrlocs de la orilla. Antaño un refugio pacífico en las estribaciones al este de Ventormenta, Villa del Lago se ha convertido en la frontera más asediada del reino. La guarnición de la villa en el Fuerte de Petravista fue brutalmente arrasada por orcos del clan Roca Negra que descendían desde el norte, y la hechicería oscura ha incitado a las manadas locales de gnolls Pellejo Sombrío a formar partidas de saqueo organizadas. Saboteadores Roca Negra incluso han destrozado partes del puente Sempiterno, lo que obliga al Supervisor Olento y a su cuadrilla a esforzarse por reparar el tramo bajo una constante amenaza de ataque. Con múrlocs asfixiando las orillas del lago y gnolls acechando en los pasos elevados, los defensores de Villa del Lago se encuentran al límite de su resistencia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,1,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire stands as Stormwind's eastern bulwark; if it falls to the Blackrock clan, the heartlands of Elwynn will face orcish incursions directly.",["race:Human"]="Rebuilt by the Alliance of Lordaeron following the devastation of the Second War, Lakeshire represents hard-won resilience for Stormwind refugees who refuse to flee their homeland a second time."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Civic authority rests with Magistrate Solomon, who directs town administration from the town hall. Local defense and policing fall under Marshal Marris and the battered remnants of the town guard.",["al"]={"lakeshire leader","who is in charge of lakeshire","magistrate of lakeshire"},["q"]="Who governs Lakeshire?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's forces are thinly stretched dealing with regional unrest, while royal councilors—notably Lady Katrana Prestor—have actively persuaded Highlord Bolvar Fordragon against committing standing troops to Redridge, forcing the Crown to rely on deputized adventurers instead.",["al"]={"why no stormwind reinforcements","stormwind army lakeshire","why is lakeshire abandoned"},["q"]="Why won't Stormwind send soldiers to help Lakeshire?"},{["a"]="Blackrock orcs damaged the massive stone bridge during their raids across the lake, severely disrupting trade and transport. Foreman Oslow oversees repairs, though missing tools and ongoing attacks keep work proceeding at a crawl.",["al"]={"broken bridge redridge","who broke everstill bridge","foreman oslow bridge"},["q"]="What happened to the Everstill Bridge?"},{["a"]="The town faces a three-front siege: Blackrock orcs occupying Stonewatch Keep to the east, Shadowhide gnolls directed by the rogue sorcerer Morganth in the northern hills, and aggressive murlocs infesting the waters and banks of Lake Everstill.",["al"]={"who is attacking lakeshire","redridge threats","lakeshire enemies"},["q"]="What threats currently surround the town?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock orcs","everstill bridge","lake everstill","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","marshal marris","redridge","stonewatch"},["n"]="Lakeshire",["s"]="Lakeshire is the primary human settlement in the Redridge Mountains, nestled along the northern shores of Lake Everstill. Led by Magistrate Solomon and guarded by Marshal Marris, the picturesque town is currently on the brink of collapse due to relentless assaults by Blackrock orcs, aggressive gnoll packs, and shoreline murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Once a peaceful haven in the foothills east of Stormwind, Lakeshire has become the kingdom's most embattled frontier. The town's garrison at Stonewatch Keep was brutally overrun by Blackrock clan orcs sweeping down from the north, and dark wizardry has riled local Shadowhide gnoll packs into organized raiding parties. Blackrock saboteurs have even shattered parts of the Everstill Bridge, leaving Foreman Oslow and his crew struggling to repair the span while under constant threat of attack. With murlocs choking the lake's shores and gnolls stalking the high passes, Lakeshire's defenders are stretched to their breaking point.",["t"]="A Town Under Siege"},{["b"]="Despite Magistrate Solomon's repeated and desperate pleas sent across the mountains, Stormwind City has provided virtually no military support. The kingdom's resources are drained by internal strife, and royal councilors dismiss Redridge's plight as exaggerated border skirmishes. Dwarven reinforcements dispatched from Ironforge were ambushed and vanished in the Burning Steppes, leaving Marshal Marris and his handful of remaining guards to hold the barricades alone. Lakeshire now survives solely on the courage of roving mercenaries and freelance adventurers hired straight out of the town hall.",["t"]="Abandoned by the Crown"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeshire-inn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,263,18.532.0,20.514.0,45.203.0,53.255.0,23.229.0,42.161.0",["h"]="07ccf1",["n"]="posada de Villa del Lago",["s"]="posada de Villa del Lago. La posada de Villa del Lago es el centro social y el principal refugio del asediado pueblo de Villa del Lago. Situada en el corazón de las Montañas Crestagrana, ofrece calidez, cerveza y un alojamiento seguro tanto para los lugareños como para los cansados viajeros que se enfrentan a los peligros de los alrededores. Emplazada a orillas del Lago Sempiterno, la posada de Villa del Lago brinda un breve respiro frente a las bandas de gnolls y orcos Roca Negra que acosan al pueblo. A pesar de la situación militar cada vez más desesperada de Villa del Lago, la taberna conserva un ambiente acogedor y animado. El Posadero Daniels y la tabernera Brianna atienden a vecinos y viajeros, sirviendo jarras de cerveza, vino y platos calientes. Es un punto de encuentro vital donde la gente del pueblo intercambia noticias, ahoga sus penas y busca mercenarios que ayuden a defender la frontera oriental del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Lakeshire Inn is an indispensable stronghold of Alliance hospitality, serving as the staging ground for anyone fighting to protect Stormwind's vulnerable eastern flank.",["profession:Cooking"]="The common room is a lively spot to procure culinary staples, local recipes, and fresh drink from Barkeep Daniels while traveling through the mountains."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The inn functions as the primary rest stop in Redridge. Innkeeper Brianna binds hearthstones and rents rooms to weary travelers, while Barkeep Daniels supplies refreshments, food, and drink for the road.",["al"]={"lakeshire inn services","what can I do at lakeshire inn","innkeeper lakeshire"},["q"]="What services does the Lakeshire Inn provide?"},{["a"]="With orcs from the Blackrock clan descending from the northern crags and gnolls raiding local farms, townspeople and displaced settlers seek safety within the town center. The tavern provides both physical shelter and a place to share news of the defense.",["al"]={"why is lakeshire inn full","lakeshire refugees inn","redridge tavern crowd"},["q"]="Why is the inn so crowded despite the nearby attacks?"},{["a"]="Wiley the Black is a somber local figure found seated inside the inn. He keeps a sharp eye on the threats facing Lakeshire and provides insight and tasks to capable adventurers looking to push back the enemy presence in Redridge.",["al"]={"wiley the black","guy in lakeshire tavern","wiley npc"},["q"]="Who is Wiley the Black?"},{["a"]="The inn sits right near the western entrance of Lakeshire along the northern bank of Lake Everstill, just off the main road leading into town from Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"where is lakeshire inn","lakeshire tavern location","find lakeshire inn"},["q"]="Where is the inn located within Lakeshire?"}},["kw"]={"barkeep daniels","darcy parker","innkeeper brianna","lake everstill","lakeshire inn","redridge inn","wiley the black","yorus barleybrew"},["n"]="Lakeshire Inn",["s"]="The Lakeshire Inn is the social hub and primary refuge in the beleaguered town of Lakeshire. Situated in the heart of the Redridge Mountains, it provides warmth, ale, and safe lodging for local townsfolk and weary travelers contending with the surrounding perils.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Perched on the shore of Lake Everstill, the Lakeshire Inn offers a brief respite from the gnoll bands and Blackrock orcs pressing in on the town. Despite Lakeshire's increasingly desperate military situation, the tavern maintains a cozy, bustling atmosphere. Barkeep Daniels and Innkeeper Brianna attend to the locals and travelers, serving up flagons of ale, wine, and warm meals. It is a vital meeting point where townspeople trade news, drown their sorrows, and seek hired blades to help defend the eastern border of the kingdom.",["t"]="A Beacon of Warmth"},{["b"]="Beyond ordinary patrons nursing drinks at the counter, the inn draws a variety of colorful figures. Wiley the Black watches the room from a table, keeping his own counsel and keeping tabs on regional dangers. Traveling brewers like Yorus Barleybrew make stops here, while Darcy Parker and other townsfolk frequent the common room. For adventurers venturing further into the jagged peaks or heading south toward Duskwood, the inn is the final bastion of civilization and safety before entering contested wilderness.",["t"]="Patrons and Whispers"}}}}}
t["subzone:lakeshire-town-hall"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,255,27.550.0,27.207.0,40.183.0,50.234.0,44.141.0,46.170.0",["h"]="167b20",["n"]="ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago",["s"]="ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago. ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago sirve como sede administrativa de las Montañas Crestagrana, erigiéndose en el corazón del asentamiento junto al lago. En su interior, el Magistrado Salomón supervisa el gobierno local mientras lidia con las incesantes amenazas de los orcos Roca Negra y los gnolls. ayuntamiento de Villa del Lago es una envejecida estructura de piedra que ha sido reformada con esmero en múltiples ocasiones a lo largo de los años. Situada de forma prominente en Villa del Lago, alberga al Magistrado Salomón, un líder civil amable y dedicado con la tarea de mantener el orden en los confines orientales del Reino de Ventormenta. Con los recursos militares de Ventormenta al límite y la ayuda real siendo escasa, el ayuntamiento ha pasado de ser una tranquila oficina administrativa a un activo centro de mando donde se tramitan a diario peticiones desesperadas de defensores voluntarios y mercenarios.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="Lakeshire Town Hall represents the eastern frontier of the Alliance in Redridge, standing as a beleaguered outpost desperately holding the line without royal support from Stormwind.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, this refurbished hall reflects both the enduring spirit of rural settlements and the frustrating abandonment felt by regional administrators when the capital turns a blind eye."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Magistrate Solomon oversees the town hall. He is a kind and well-meaning administrator who serves as the primary governing authority for Lakeshire and the surrounding Redridge valley.",["al"]={"who leads lakeshire","magistrate solomon","who is in town hall"},["q"]="Who is in charge at Lakeshire Town Hall?"},{["a"]="Lakeshire faces severe, mounting threats from local gnoll packs and hostile Blackrock orc warbands. Because Stormwind has provided minimal military reinforcements, Magistrate Solomon must hire passing adventurers to defend the region.",["al"]={"why does solomon need help","lakeshire problems","why are there so many quests here"},["q"]="Why is the town hall seeking so much outside help?"},{["a"]="The town's problems with gnolls and Blackrock orcs have put Solomon in a desperate position. He readily accepts aid from helpful adventurers.",["al"]={"why does solomon accept aid","lakeshire adventurers","town hall help"},["q"]="Why does Solomon accept help from travelers?"},{["a"]="Yes, it is an older building that has survived turbulent decades and undergone diligent repairs and refurbishments to keep it functioning as the civic center of Redridge.",["al"]={"town hall age","how old is lakeshire town hall","town hall history"},["q"]="Has Lakeshire Town Hall stood for a long time?"}},["kw"]={"blackrock","gnolls","lakeshire","magistrate solomon","redridge","redridge mountains","stormwind","town hall"},["n"]="Lakeshire Town Hall",["s"]="Lakeshire Town Hall serves as the administrative seat of the Redridge Mountains, standing at the heart of the lakeside settlement. Inside, Magistrate Solomon oversees local governance while wrestling with relentless threats from Blackrock orcs and gnolls.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Lakeshire Town Hall is an aging stone structure that has been diligently refurbished multiple times over the years. Positioned prominently within Lakeshire, it houses Magistrate Solomon, a kind and dedicated civil leader tasked with maintaining order in the eastern reaches of the Kingdom of Stormwind. With Stormwind's military resources stretched thin and royal aid scarce, the hall has transformed from a quiet administrative office into an active command center where desperate appeals for volunteer defenders and mercenaries are processed daily.",["t"]="Seat of Redridge Governance"},{["b"]="Gnoll incursions and the encroaching Blackrock orcs have pushed Solomon to desperation. With aid scarce, the magistrate readily accepts help from independent adventurers who come through the town hall doors.",["t"]="Under Siege and Overwhelmed"}}}}}
t["subzone:library-wing-northshire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="25,224,32.500.0,34.152.0,33.189.0",["h"]="649f2a",["n"]="Ala de la Biblioteca (Villanorte)",["s"]="Ala de la Biblioteca (Villanorte). El Ala de la Biblioteca es la tranquila ala sur repleta de libros de la Abadía de Villanorte, en el Bosque de Elwynn. Sirve como santuario para eruditos, ofreciendo instrucción inicial a sacerdotes y magos novatos que se unen a la defensa de Ventormenta. Extendiéndose hacia el sur desde el salón principal de la Abadía de Villanorte, el ala de la biblioteca alberga estanterías polvorientas, atriles de estudio y tranquilos rincones dedicados a la formación intelectual y espiritual. Mientras los reclutas marciales entrenan en la Sala de Armas septentrional, los aspirantes a magos y sacerdotes se reúnen aquí para comprender los fundamentos de lo Arcano y la Luz Sagrada. En la actualidad, la Sacerdotisa Anetta guía a los sacerdotes novicios en cuestiones de fe y sanación, mientras que Khelden Bremen enseña a los magos en ciernes cómo moldear la energía elemental primigenia.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Khelden Bremen instructs novice mages within these quiet halls, teaching the foundational disciplines of fire and frost.",["class:Priest"]="Priestess Anetta resides here, offering fledgling priests their very first lessons in channeling the Holy Light to mend wounds and smite foes."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Library Wing occupies the southern section of Northshire Abbey, situated just off the Main Hall. It sits directly opposite the martial Hall of Arms.",["al"]={"where is the library wing","how to find northshire library","library location northshire"},["q"]="Where is the Library Wing located?"},{["a"]="It serves as the academic and spiritual center of Northshire Abbey, dedicated to scholarly research, magical instruction, and prayer for recruits training to serve the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["al"]={"why does northshire abbey have a library","library wing purpose"},["q"]="What is the purpose of this wing?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","khelden bremen","library wing","mage trainer","northshire","northshire abbey","priest trainer","priestess anetta"},["n"]="Library Wing (Northshire)",["s"]="The Library Wing is the quiet, book-lined southern wing of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. It serves as a sanctuary for scholars, offering early instruction to fledgling priests and mages joining the defense of Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Branching south from the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey, the Library Wing houses dusty shelves, study lecterns, and quiet alcoves dedicated to intellectual and spiritual training. While martial recruits drill in the northern Hall of Arms, aspiring mages and priests gather here to grasp the fundamentals of the Arcane and the Holy Light. Currently, Priestess Anetta guides novice priests in matters of faith and healing, while Khelden Bremen teaches budding mages how to shape primal elemental energy.",["t"]="Haven of Arcane and Divine Study"}}}}}
t["subzone:lion-s-pride-inn"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,263,18.715.0,39.209.0,43.208.0,44.279.0,42.104.0",["h"]="fbd33d",["n"]="Posada Orgullo de León",["s"]="Posada Orgullo de León. La Posada Orgullo de León es la bulliciosa taberna y centro comunitario de Villadorada, en el Bosque de Elwynn. Regentada durante generaciones por la familia Farley, sirve como el principal lugar de descanso, sala de reuniones y casa de contratación para los viajeros que se aventuran al sur de la Ciudad de Ventormenta. Situada en la encrucijada del Bosque de Elwynn, la Posada Orgullo de León es el animado núcleo de Villadorada. Dirigida por el Tabernero Farley bajo el lema tradicional de la taberna («Paz y reposo para los cansados y ateridos»), la posada ofrece cálidos hogares, bebidas fuertes y habitaciones para los aventureros fatigados recién salidos de Villanorte. La familia de Farley ha regentado el establecimiento con orgullo durante generaciones, remontándose al reinado del rey Llane Wrynn I. Dado que Villadorada se encuentra en las rutas comerciales vitales entre Ventormenta, Páramos de Poniente, Crestagrana y el Bosque del Ocaso, la taberna sirve como un punto de encuentro indispensable donde los alguaciles de la ciudad, los artesanos locales y los instructores veteranos se reúnen para compartir noticias y contratar a los mercenarios que van de paso.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="As the main inn outside Stormwind's gates, it serves as a bustling waystation where Alliance travelers coordinate patrols and trade across the heartlands.",["race:Human"]="For humans venturing forth from Northshire Abbey, the Lion's Pride Inn is their first encounter with the broader life and troubles of the kingdom outside monastery walls."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The inn is operated by Innkeeper Farley. His family has maintained and run the Lion's Pride Inn as an above-board business for generations, dating back to before the First War in the era of King Llane Wrynn I.",["al"]={"innkeeper","who owns lions pride","who runs goldshire inn"},["q"]="Who owns and runs the Lion's Pride Inn?"},{["a"]="Beyond food, drink, and lodging, the Lion's Pride Inn houses various class trainers, visiting merchants, and local quest givers seeking aid with the gnoll, kobold, and bandit problems troubling Elwynn Forest.",["al"]={"trainers","what is inside","amenities"},["q"]="What services are available inside the inn?"},{["a"]="Positioned directly at the Goldshire crossroads just south of Stormwind, the inn is the primary rest stop for travelers moving between the capital, Westfall, and the Redridge Mountains. It is naturally the first major hub young adventurers visit upon departing Northshire Valley.",["al"]={"why so popular","goldshire crossroads","importance of lions pride"},["q"]="Why is the inn such a central hub in Elwynn?"},{["a"]="According to Innkeeper Farley, the inn's founding motto is 'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold.'",["al"]={"inn motto","motto"},["q"]="What is the motto of the Lion's Pride Inn?"}},["kw"]={"elwynn forest","farley","goldshire","goldshire inn","innkeeper farley","lion's pride inn","lions pride"},["n"]="Lion's Pride Inn",["s"]="The Lion's Pride Inn is the bustling tavern and community center of Goldshire in Elwynn Forest. Kept for generations by the Farley family, it serves as the primary resting place, meeting hall, and hiring house for travelers venturing just south of Stormwind City.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Standing at the crossroads of Elwynn Forest, the Lion's Pride Inn is Goldshire's lively centerpiece. Operated by Innkeeper Farley under the tavern's traditional motto—'Rest and relaxation for the tired and cold'—the inn offers warm hearths, strong drinks, and rooms for weary adventurers fresh out of Northshire. Farley's family has managed the establishment with pride for generations, dating back through the reign of King Llane Wrynn I. Because Goldshire lies along the vital trade routes between Stormwind, Westfall, Redridge, and Duskwood, the tavern serves as an indispensable rallying point where town marshals, local crafters, and seasoned trainers gather to share news and contract passing mercenaries.",["t"]="Heart of Goldshire"}}}}}
t["subzone:long-wash"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,278,18.526.0,31.166.0,31.216.0,46.198.0,50.199.0",["h"]="7ad271",["n"]="Playa del Oleaje",["s"]="Playa del Oleaje. La Playa del Oleaje es un tramo de playa sombrío y azotado por el viento en Costa Oscura que se extiende justo al sur de Auberdine hacia las ruinas de Ameth'Aran. Lúgubre y salpicada de restos flotantes y cadáveres marinos, la costa se ha vuelto peligrosa recientemente debido a la creciente presencia de múrlocs hostiles. A pesar de su nombre, la Playa del Oleaje es en realidad el tramo diferenciado de costa más corto de Costa Oscura. Se encuentra bajo los cielos perpetuamente nublados de la región, una extensión de arena húmeda repleta de restos flotantes, madera a la deriva varada y cadáveres de criaturas marinas arrastrados por el Mar de la Bruma. Mientras los cangrejos y caracoles locales rebuscan entre el oleaje, los viajeros que se dirigen al sur desde Auberdine deben avanzar con cautela: varias tribus de múrlocs han establecido campamentos a la orilla del agua, atacando con agresividad a cualquiera que invada su territorio carroñero.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei of Auberdine, the encroaching murlocs along the Long Wash represent another sign of unsettling imbalance creeping right up to the doorstep of their main port."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Long Wash stretches along the coastline of Darkshore immediately south of Auberdine, extending down until it lies roughly west of the ancient ruins of Ameth'Aran.",["al"]={"long wash location","where is long wash","how to find long wash"},["q"]="Where is the Long Wash located?"},{["a"]="A 'wash' is an archaic term referring to the portion of a shore swept and washed over by ocean waves. Ironically, despite being named the Long Wash, it is actually the shortest distinct stretch of beach in Darkshore.",["al"]={"why long wash","long wash meaning","what does wash mean"},["q"]="Why is it called the Long Wash?"},{["a"]="The main danger along the Long Wash comes from aggressive murloc clans that have begun gathering in greater numbers along the coastline, alongside territorial tide crawlers and other beach wildlife.",["al"]={"dangers in long wash","long wash mobs","what lives in long wash"},["q"]="What threats can be found along the Long Wash?"},{["a"]="The rough surf of the Veiled Sea and the encroaching corruption affecting the coastal waters of Darkshore regularly wash up debris, ship drift, and dying marine life onto the damp sands of the shore.",["al"]={"dead animals long wash","beached creatures darkshore beach","flotsam on the shore"},["q"]="Why are there so many dead creatures on the beach?"}},["kw"]={"ameth'aran","auberdine","darkshore","long wash","murloc","tide crawler","veiled sea"},["n"]="Long Wash",["s"]="The Long Wash is a bleak, windswept stretch of beach in Darkshore running just south of Auberdine toward the ruins of Ameth'Aran. Gloomy and scattered with marine carcasses and flotsam, the shoreline has recently grown dangerous due to an increasing presence of hostile murlocs.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Despite its name, the Long Wash is actually the shortest distinct stretch of coastline in Darkshore. It sits under the region's perpetual overcast skies, an expanse of damp sand littered with flotsam, beached driftwood, and the carcasses of sea creatures washed up by the Veiled Sea. While local crabs and snails comb through the surf, travelers southward from Auberdine must tread cautiously: murloc tribes have established camps along the water's edge, aggressively attacking anyone encroaching on their scavenged territory.",["t"]="A Gloomy Shoreline"}}}}}
t["subzone:longshore"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="9,255,23.513.0,34.260.0,23.284.0,44.239.0,34.262.0",["h"]="0e8ae3",["n"]="Playa Larga",["s"]="Playa Larga. Playa Larga es la amplia costa arenosa que se extiende a lo largo de todo el límite occidental de Páramos de Poniente. A pesar de su vasta y pintoresca extensión, la orilla es célebremente peligrosa debido a las densas poblaciones de múrlocs agresivos y a los naufragios dispersos frente a la costa. A lo largo de todo el extremo occidental de Páramos de Poniente, Playa Larga es una de las playas continuas más extensas de los Reinos del Este. Sin embargo, ofrece poca paz a los viajeros. Los múrlocs costeros dominan el oleaje, liderados por notorios terrores como el Viejo Ojosombrío, mientras que los restos de navíos hundidos —incluidos destructores élficos en ruinas— salpican las aguas poco profundas. Cerca de los confines meridionales, colonos aislados como Daphne Fontana luchan contra los bandidos saqueadores de los Defias, a la vista del Faro de Poniente al otro lado del agua.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Alliance druids must brave the depths off the northwestern Longshore, locating a lockbox hidden near a sunken wreck to assemble the pendant required for their aquatic form.",["class:Paladin"]="Paladins following the guidance of Duthorian Rall in Stormwind are sent south to Daphne Stilwell's homestead on Longshore, proving their valor by shielding an innocent farmer from Defias raiders."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shoreline is infested with aggressive murloc tribes that roam unchecked across the sands, ambushing anyone who strays too close to the surf. In addition to the murlocs, the southern end of the beach is troubled by Defias bandits raiding coastal homesteads.",["al"]={"why are there so many murlocs","longshore hazards","is longshore safe"},["q"]="Why is the Longshore so dangerous?"},{["a"]="Daphne Stilwell is a lone settler maintaining an isolated farm on the southwestern stretch of the Longshore. Her vulnerable position makes her a frequent target for raids by the Defias Brotherhood, prompting the Knights of the Silver Hand to dispatch paladin initiates to her defense.",["al"]={"daphne stilwell","stilwell farm","woman on the beach"},["q"]="Who is Daphne Stilwell?"},{["a"]="Numerous wrecks lie submerged off the Longshore, ranging from merchant vessels to elven destroyers lost during past naval conflicts. These underwater ruins attract scavengers, murlocs, and adventurers seeking relics lost beneath the waves.",["al"]={"elven destroyers westfall","sunken ships longshore","shipwrecks"},["q"]="What are the shipwrecks lying off the coast?"},{["a"]="Alliance druids undertake a rite known as the Trial of the Sea Lion to master their aquatic form. Part of this trial requires seeking out a submerged chest near an offshore shipwreck along northwestern Longshore to retrieve the Half Pendant of Aquatic Endurance.",["al"]={"druid quest longshore","strange lockbox westfall","half pendant of aquatic endurance"},["q"]="Why do druids visit the Longshore?"}},["kw"]={"aquatic form","daphne stilwell","longshore","murloc","old murk-eye","shipwrecks","westfall","westfall lighthouse"},["n"]="Longshore",["s"]="The Longshore is the expansive sandy coastline stretching along the entire western edge of Westfall. Despite its vast and scenic expanse, the shore is notoriously hazardous due to thick populations of aggressive murlocs and scattered wrecks off the coast.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running the full western length of Westfall, the Longshore is one of the widest unbroken beaches in the Eastern Kingdoms. Yet it offers little peace to travelers. Coastal murlocs dominate the surf, led by notorious terrors like Old Murk-Eye, while the remnants of sunken vessels—including ruined elven destroyers—litter the shallows. Near the southern reaches, isolated settlers like Daphne Stilwell struggle against marauding Defias bandits, standing within sight of the Westfall Lighthouse across the water.",["t"]="A Treacherous Coastline"}}}}}
t["subzone:lordamere-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,349,28.598.0,19.525.0,51.222.0,51.207.0,27.184.0,30.150.0",["h"]="62ed52",["n"]="Lago Lordamere",["s"]="Lago Lordamere. El Lago Lordamere es una de las mayores masas de agua dulce de los Reinos del Este, bordeada por los Claros de Tirisfal, el Bosque de Argénteos y las Montañas de Alterac. En su día fue el bullicioso corazón acuático de la civilización humana en el norte, pero sus frías aguas e islas están ahora atormentadas por nigromantes de la Plaga, múrlocs salvajes y la sombra invasora de los no-muertos. En la época dorada de la Alianza de Lordaeron, el Lago Lordamere se encontraba en la encrucijada del poder humano. La Capital de Lordaeron custodiaba sus costas septentrionales, la ciudad-estado hechicera de Dalaran se alzaba cerca de su límite meridional y el reino de Alterac bordeaba su escarpado extremo oriental. Barcos mercantes y embarcaciones pesqueras surcaban antaño sin temor su amplia y neblinosa extensión. Tras la devastación de la Tercera Guerra, el lago pasó de ser un centro neurálgico del comercio a una barrera natural que separaba las tierras de Tirisfal y Argénteos, en manos de los Renegados, de las traicioneras alturas de Alterac.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Human"]="The quiet, foggy waters of Lordamere are a somber reminder of the ruined glory of the northern human kingdoms, which once traded freely across its shores.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, Lordamere Lake serves as both a defensive moat protecting Tirisfal and an active frontline where Scourge remnants on Fenris Isle must be purged."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Lordamere Lake was bordered by three major human kingdoms during the height of the Alliance of Lordaeron: the Kingdom of Lordaeron to the north and west, Dalaran to the south, and Alterac along its eastern mountain bluffs.",["al"]={"who lived on lordamere lake","lordamere lake history","kingdoms around lordamere"},["q"]="What kingdoms historically bordered Lordamere Lake?"},{["a"]="Fenris Isle is currently held by agents of the Scourge under the command of the necromancer Thule Ravenclaw, though they face relentless assaults from the Forsaken and constant pressure from ravenous worgen.",["al"]={"who is on fenris isle","fenris island lordamere","fenris isle ruler"},["q"]="Who controls Fenris Isle in the middle of the lake?"},{["a"]="The Dawning Isles are a cluster of small islands situated in the eastern portion of Lordamere Lake, east of Fenris Isle. They have been overrun and claimed by hostile Vile Fin murlocs.",["al"]={"dawning isles location","islands in lordamere lake","dawning isles monsters"},["q"]="What are the Dawning Isles?"},{["a"]="The lake was named in conjunction with the nearby Capital City and kingdom of Lordaeron, which took their name from the ancient human general Lordain.",["al"]={"lordamere name origin","why is it called lordamere"},["q"]="How did the lake get its name?"}},["kw"]={"alterac mountains","dawning isles","fenris isle","lake lordamere","lordamere lake","silverpine forest","thule ravenclaw","tirisfal glades","vile fin"},["n"]="Lordamere Lake",["s"]="Lordamere Lake is one of the largest bodies of freshwater in the Eastern Kingdoms, bordered by Tirisfal Glades, Silverpine Forest, and the Alterac Mountains. Once the bustling aquatic heart of human civilization in the north, its cold waters and islands are now haunted by Scourge necromancers, feral murlocs, and the spreading shadow of the undead.",["sec"]={{["b"]="In the golden age of the Alliance of Lordaeron, Lordamere Lake sat at the crossroads of human power. The Capital City of Lordaeron guarded its northern shores, the sorcerous city-state of Dalaran rose near its southern reach, and the kingdom of Alterac lined its mountainous eastern edge. Merchant vessels and fishing boats once crossed its broad, mist-covered expanse without fear. Following the devastation of the Third War, the lake was transformed from a hub of commerce into a natural barrier dividing the Forsaken-held lands of Tirisfal and Silverpine from the treacherous heights of Alterac.",["t"]="Heart of the Fallen Kingdoms"},{["b"]="Today, navigating the dark waters of Lordamere is fraught with peril. At the center of the lake sits Fenris Isle, where Scourge necromancer Thule Ravenclaw and his undead thralls hold out against the Forsaken, while vicious worgen prowl the vicinity. Further east lie the Dawning Isles, completely overrun by aggressive Vile Fin murlocs. From the ruins around Dalaran to the shoreline of the Undercity, the lake is no longer a peaceful highway, but a drowned frontier contested by remnant monsters and the armies of the dead.",["t"]="A Contested Expanse"}}}}}
t["subzone:lushwater-oasis"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,364,22.501.0,53.138.0,29.174.0,30.153.0,39.206.0",["h"]="1b8712",["n"]="Oasis Aguaverde",["s"]="Oasis Aguaverde. El Oasis Aguaverde es uno de los tres abrevaderos rebosantes de vida ubicados en los áridos Baldíos, situado justo al sur de El Cruce. A pesar de su apariencia exuberante, el oasis entraña un gran peligro: está infestado de agresivos centauros Kolkar y alberga la entrada a las Cuevas de los Lamentos. Sus aguas contaminadas son bien conocidas por los pescadores que buscan el peculiar Pez descarriado. Situado a una corta marcha al sur de El Cruce, el Oasis Aguaverde ofrece un respiro engañoso en medio de la extensión calcinada por el sol de Los Baldíos. Aunque sus copas de palmeras y sus manantiales de agua dulce atraen a bestias sedientas de toda la sabana, los centauros Kolkar reclaman sus orillas, al acecho para masacrar tanto a las presas como a los viajeros incautos. El oasis es también la puerta de entrada a las Cuevas de los Lamentos, cuyas extensas redes subterráneas filtran energías corruptoras en las pozas superiores, engendrando una fauna antinatural y extrañas mutaciones.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Druid"]="Lushwater Oasis exhibits a troubling, unnatural overgrowth driven by the twisted energies escaping the nearby Wailing Caverns.",["profession:Cooking"]="The pools here are among the few waters where anglers can land Deviate Fish, a vital ingredient prized across Kalimdor for preparing Savory Deviate Delights."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The entrance to the Wailing Caverns cavern system lies carved into the natural rock faces overlooking the eastern side of Lushwater Oasis.",["al"]={"where is wc","wc cave entrance","wailing caverns entrance"},["q"]="Where is the entrance to the Wailing Caverns located?"},{["a"]="The Kolkar centaur maintain a dominant presence throughout the oasis, using the lush cover to hunt passing wildlife and attack travelers making their way from the Crossroads.",["al"]={"who lives at lushwater oasis","lushwater enemies","centaur at the oasis"},["q"]="Who controls Lushwater Oasis?"},{["a"]="The deep energies leaking from the Wailing Caverns have corrupted the waterways across the oasis, causing local fish to mutate into unusual Deviate Fish.",["al"]={"deviate fish location","why deviate fish","mutated fish oasis"},["q"]="Why are the fish here strange?"},{["a"]="During the orcs' Long March through the Barrens alongside the tauren, Thrall led his troops through the region's scattered oases to secure vital drinking water while fending off relentless centaur ambushes.",["al"]={"thrall long march oasis","orcs in barrens oasis"},["q"]="Did Thrall's Horde travel through here?"}},["kw"]={"crossroads","deviate fish","kolkar","lushwater oasis","the barrens","wailing caverns"},["n"]="Lushwater Oasis",["s"]="Lushwater Oasis is one of the three life-giving watering holes nestled in the arid Barrens, located just south of the Crossroads. Despite its verdant appearance, the oasis is fraught with danger, infested by aggressive Kolkar centaur and harboring the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. Its tainted waters are well-known to anglers seeking the peculiar Deviate Fish.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated a short march south of the Crossroads, Lushwater Oasis offers a deceptive respite amid the sun-bleached expanse of the Barrens. While its palm canopies and fresh springs draw thirsty beasts from across the savanna, Kolkar centaur claim the banks, lying in wait to butcher both game and unwary travelers. The oasis is also the gateway to the Wailing Caverns, whose sprawling underground networks seep corruptive energies into the pools above, breeding unnatural wildlife and bizarre mutations.",["t"]="A Precarious Sanctuary"}}}}}
t["subzone:maclure-vineyards"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="17,281,16.441.0,19.440.1,46.246.0,23.216.0,35.187.0,34.148.0",["h"]="031d51",["n"]="Los Viñedos de Maclure",["s"]="Los Viñedos de Maclure. Los Viñedos de Maclure son una extensa finca agrícola situada en el sur del Bosque de Elwynn, propiedad de la familia Maclure. Aunque es conocida por producir uvas y vino para el reino de Ventormenta, la granja es igualmente famosa por una amarga y continua disputa con sus vecinos, la familia Stonefield. Enclavados en las exuberantes colinas del sur del Bosque de Elwynn, Los Viñedos de Maclure deberían ser un remanso de paz dedicado a la viticultura y la agricultura. En su lugar, el trabajo diario se ve ensombrecido por una encarnizada y prolongada rivalidad con los Stonefield, situados al final del camino. Las acusaciones de robo y el rencor están muy arraigados entre ambas familias, lo que mantiene los ánimos encendidos incluso cuando problemas comunes, como jabalíes hambrientos al acecho y kóbolds invasores, amenazan ambos hogares.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The estate serves as an important breadbasket and vineyard supplying the nearby settlements of Goldshire and Stormwind City with food and spirits.",["race:Human"]="For humans of Stormwind, the vineyard feud is a classic example of countryside stubbornness, reminding travelers that even within the heartland, neighbors often bicker over fences while larger perils loom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The rivalry is a long-standing rural feud built on years of mistrust, petty accusations, and stubborn pride. Neither family trusts the other an inch, blaming each other for lost goods and livestock, though neither has outright proof of foul play.",["al"]={"maclure stonefield feud","why do they hate each other","family feud"},["q"]="Why are the Maclures and Stonefields fighting?"},{["a"]="Maybell is the daughter of the Maclure household. She has secretly fallen in love with Tommy Joe Stonefield, defying her family's bitter hatred of their neighbors in the hope of finding a way for them to be together.",["al"]={"maybell","maclure daughter"},["q"]="Who is Maybell Maclure?"},{["a"]="Aside from family disputes, the vineyards are plagued by ravenous wild boars trampling the crops and vines, as well as wandering kobolds raiding nearby fields from surrounding gold mines.",["al"]={"vineyard dangers","boars at maclure"},["q"]="What threats do the vineyards face?"},{["a"]="The Maclure family cultivates grapevines to supply wine and fresh fruit to tavern-keepers and merchants throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind City.",["al"]={"what grows here","maclure crops"},["q"]="What do the Maclures produce here?"}},["kw"]={"boars","elwynn","gerard","maclure","maybell","stonefield","vineyard","wine"},["n"]="Maclure Vineyards",["s"]="Maclure Vineyards is a sprawling agricultural estate in southern Elwynn Forest owned by the Maclure family. While known for producing grapes and wine for the kingdom of Stormwind, the farmstead is equally infamous for an ongoing, bitter feud with the neighboring Stonefield family.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Nestled in the lush hills of southern Elwynn Forest, the Maclure Vineyards should be a peaceful haven of winecraft and farming. Instead, everyday labor is overshadowed by a vicious, long-standing rivalry with the Stonefields just down the road. Accusations of theft and bad blood run deep between the households, keeping tempers flaring even as common troubles—like hungry prowling boars and encroaching kobolds—threaten both homesteads.",["t"]="A Bitter Harvest"},{["b"]="Despite the fierce animosity between the two patriarchs, young love has crossed the boundary lines. Maybell Maclure and Tommy Joe Stonefield have fallen secretly in love, meeting in hidden groves away from their parents' suspicious eyes. Those passing through the vineyards often find themselves drawn into running secret messages, resolving petty grievances, and trying to help the young couple escape the shadow of their families' grudge.",["t"]="A Forbidden Romance"}}}}}
t["subzone:maestra-s-post"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,306,15.496.0,21.462.0,32.125.0,16.155.0,41.223.0,33.186.0",["h"]="99def9",["n"]="Atalaya de Maestra",["s"]="Atalaya de Maestra. La Atalaya de Maestra es un pequeño asentamiento de la Alianza en el oeste de Vallefresno, encaramado junto al camino al noroeste de Astranaar y al sur de Las Ruinas de Ordil'Aran. Custodiada por centinelas de los elfos de la noche y hogar de una inusual presencia humana en el antiguo bosque de Kalimdor, sirve como puesto de vigilancia avanzada contra las amenazas invasoras. Situada bajo el dosel del oeste de Vallefresno, la Atalaya de Maestra consta de una esbelta torre de los elfos de la noche y un pabellón abierto. Se erige como un punto de paso esencial para los viajeros que marchan entre la costa de Costa Oscura y el núcleo mayor de Astranaar. A pesar de su tranquila arquitectura élfica, el puesto de avanzada permanece perpetuamente en alerta. Las centinelas locales vigilan con recelo la espesura circundante, donde los fúrbolgs corruptos se agitan y los movimientos cercanos de la Horda amenazan constantemente las líneas de suministro de la Alianza.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers leaving the safety of Darkshore, this outpost represents your first friendly welcome and fortified sanctuary in the contested forests of Ashenvale.",["race:NightElf"]="The post demonstrates the burgeoning partnership of the new Alliance, showing Sentinels sharing hearth and watch duty with the younger races of the Eastern Kingdoms."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is located in western Ashenvale, situated along the road northwest of Astranaar and just south of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran.",["al"]={"maestra's post location","where is maestras post","find maestras post"},["q"]="Where is Maestra's Post located?"},{["a"]="The post takes its name from Moon Priestess Maestra, a night elf figure of reverence, though the priestess herself is not currently present at the outpost.",["al"]={"who is maestra","moon priestess maestra","who was maestra"},["q"]="Who was Maestra?"},{["a"]="Following the third war and the night elves joining the Alliance, travelers and warriors like Feero Ironhand and Delgren the Purifier have ventured into Kalimdor to offer aid and strengthen ties with their night elf allies.",["al"]={"why are humans in ashenvale","feero ironhand why here","delgren the purifier why here"},["q"]="Why are there humans at an elven outpost?"},{["a"]="The outpost must contend with corrupted furbolg clans lurking in the surrounding woodland, as well as scouting parties and incursions from the nearby Horde forces pushing into Ashenvale.",["al"]={"who attacks maestras post","dangers at maestras post"},["q"]="What threats face Maestra's Post?"}},["kw"]={"ashenvale","delgren the purifier","feero ironhand","maestra's post","maestras post","ordil'aran","sentinels"},["n"]="Maestra's Post",["s"]="Maestra's Post is a small Alliance settlement in western Ashenvale, perched along the road northwest of Astranaar and south of the Ruins of Ordil'Aran. Guarded by night elven Sentinels and hosting a rare human presence in Kalimdor's ancient forest, it serves as a forward watch against encroaching threats.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Positioned under the canopy of western Ashenvale, Maestra's Post consists of a slender night elven tower and an open lodge. It sits as an essential waypoint for travelers marching between the coast of Darkshore and the larger hub of Astranaar. Despite its tranquil elven architecture, the outpost stands perpetually on edge. The local Sentinels keep a wary eye on the surrounding wilderness, where corrupted furbolg stir and nearby Horde movements constantly threaten the Alliance's supply lines.",["t"]="A Forward Watch"},{["b"]="Unlike many insular night elf enclaves deep within the woods, Maestra's Post is notable for housing a handful of human allies. Figures such as Feero Ironhand and Delgren the Purifier dwell alongside the Sentinels here, lending their martial strength and devotion to the holy Light in service to the broader Alliance. Their presence makes this remote campsite one of the earliest meeting grounds between the eastern kingdoms and the ancient defenders of Kalimdor.",["t"]="An Alliance Gathering"}}}}}
t["subzone:mage-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="12,378,21.510.0,27.491.1,29.257.0,45.246.0,43.254.0,34.193.0",["h"]="6e7855",["n"]="Barrio de los Magos",["s"]="Barrio de los Magos. El Barrio de los Magos conforma el corazón arcano de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, situado al otro lado de los canales, en la esquina suroeste de la capital. Elevándose sobre sus calles empedradas y sus esotéricas tiendas especializadas se alza el Sagrario del Mago, donde los evocadores del reino perfeccionan su arte. Bajo la superficie erudita del distrito también yacen sombríos rincones que albergan a practicantes de artes mucho más oscuras. Accesible mediante puentes que cruzan los canales desde la Plaza de la Catedral o el Distrito de Mercaderes, el Barrio de los Magos atiende por completo las necesidades místicas de la Alianza. En torno a la aguja del Sagrario del Mago, lanzadores de conjuros humanos y aliados se reúnen para estudiar el tejido de la magia arcana e instruir a aprendices. Las calles circundantes están repletas de proveedores de telas para sastrería, componentes, suministros alquímicos y bastones encantados, creando un distrito insular dedicado a la investigación y a la defensa del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The district serves as your central home in Stormwind, offering master trainers and spell reagents inside the Wizard's Sanctum.",["class:Warlock"]="Beneath the public guise of The Slaughtered Lamb tavern lies the hidden coven where practitioners of the dark arts convene to train and summon minions in secret."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Wizard's Sanctum is the prominent tower dominating the Mage Quarter. It serves as the primary academy, library, and training grounds for Stormwind's mages, housing scholars, mystic trainers, and defensive spellcasters tasked with protecting the capital.",["al"]={"mage tower","wizards sanctum","mage sanctum stormwind"},["q"]="What is the Wizard's Sanctum?"},{["a"]="Warlocks gather secretly beneath The Slaughtered Lamb, an unassuming tavern in the quarter. Down in its crypts and hidden cellars, practitioners of fel magic can study dark rituals, summon demons, and train outside the scrutiny of the city guard.",["al"]={"warlock trainer location","slaughtered lamb basement","stormwind warlock trainers"},["q"]="Where can warlocks train in the Mage Quarter?"},{["a"]="The district is filled with specialty trades catering to casters and crafters. Visitors can find tailoring shops like Duncan's Textiles and Larson Clothiers, alchemy and herbalism merchants, enchanting vendors, pyrotechnic suppliers, and staff merchants.",["al"]={"mage quarter vendors","what shops are here","stores in mage quarter"},["q"]="What kind of shops are in the Mage Quarter?"},{["a"]="The Mage Quarter occupies the southwestern corner of Stormwind City. It can be accessed directly by crossing the bridges that span the Canals from either the Trade District or Cathedral Square.",["al"]={"where is mage quarter","how to get to mage quarter","directions to mage quarter"},["q"]="How do you reach the Mage Quarter?"}},["kw"]={"arcane","blue recluse","canals","mage quarter","slaughtered lamb","stormwind","wizard's sanctum"},["n"]="Mage Quarter",["s"]="The Mage Quarter forms the arcane heart of Stormwind City, resting across the canals in the capital's southwestern corner. Towering over its cobblestone streets and esoteric specialty shops stands the Wizard's Sanctum, where the kingdom's conjurers hone their craft. Beneath the district's scholarly surface also lie shadowy recesses, harboring practitioners of far darker arts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Reachable by bridges crossing the canals from Cathedral Square or the Trade District, the Mage Quarter caters entirely to the mystical needs of the Alliance. Centered around the spire of the Wizard's Sanctum, human and allied spellcasters gather to study the weave of arcane magic and train apprentices. The surrounding streets are crowded with purveyors of tailoring cloth, reagents, alchemical supplies, and enchanted staves, creating an insular district dedicated to research and the defense of the kingdom.",["t"]="Sanctum of the Arcane"},{["b"]="Not all sorcery practiced in the quarter is approved by the kingdom's high conjurers. While establishments like The Blue Recluse offer quiet refuge for scholars, the infamous Slaughtered Lamb tavern conceals a covert coven of warlocks in its subterranean crypts. There, out of sight of the city guard and the holy eyes of Cathedral Square, demonologists study forbidden fel rites and bind otherworldly entities while masquerading beneath the district's general tolerance of mystic anomalies.",["t"]="Secrets Beneath the Surface"}}}}}
t["subzone:magic-quarter"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,245,23.561.0,32.481.0,41.233.0,53.301.0,40.165.0,35.117.0",["h"]="d5322b",["n"]="Barrio de la Magia",["s"]="Barrio de la Magia. El Barrio de la Magia es el distrito noreste de Entrañas, y sirve como centro para el estudio arcano y la hechicería oscura de los Renegados. Dominado por un ominoso Templo de los Condenados, el barrio alberga a practicantes tanto de las artes arcanas como de las viles. Ocupando el cuadrante noreste de la ciudad subterránea, el Barrio de la Magia es el lugar donde los Renegados preservan su legado arcano y profundizan en metodologías más oscuras. La pieza central del distrito es un imponente Templo de los Condenados, una reliquia arquitectónica de diseño de la Plaga que ha sido reutilizada por los no-muertos de libre albedrío. Bajo sus techos abovedados y sombríos, los magos practican sutiles manipulaciones de energías mágicas junto a brujos que comulgan con entidades demoníacas, convirtiendo al barrio en el nexo de poder intelectual e investigación oculta de Lordaeron.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="The Magic Quarter is the heart of Forsaken wizardry, offering training in arcane arts and teleportation networks that link the Undercity with the wider Horde.",["class:Warlock"]="Within the dark alcoves of the Temple of the Damned, warlocks summon demonic minions and hone shadow magic far from the judgmental eyes of the Alliance."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Magic Quarter serves as the center of arcane and demonic studies for the Forsaken. It houses class trainers for mages and warlocks, portal masters connecting to other cities, and tailoring professionals who weave enchanted cloth.",["al"]={"what is magic quarter","magic quarter purpose","undercity magic district"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Magic Quarter?"},{["a"]="When the Undercity was carved out beneath the ruins of Capital City by the Scourge, they erected structures like the Temple of the Damned. When Sylvanas and her free-willed Forsaken seized the subterranean complex, they claimed these existing facilities and repurposed them for their own spellcasters.",["al"]={"temple of the damned undercity","why temple of the damned here","scourge building undercity"},["q"]="Why is there a Temple of the Damned in the Undercity?"},{["a"]="Mages, warlocks, and demon trainers instruct practitioners within the quarter, while portal specialists and tailoring artisans offer training in transport and craft.",["al"]={"trainers in magic quarter","who trains here","magic quarter classes"},["q"]="Who can be trained in the Magic Quarter?"},{["a"]="It is situated in the northeastern quadrant of the Undercity, directly across the central ring from the Apothecarium.",["al"]={"where is magic quarter","magic quarter location","find magic quarter"},["q"]="Where is the Magic Quarter located?"}},["kw"]={"forsaken","mage","magic quarter","portal trainer","tailoring","temple of the damned","undercity","warlock"},["n"]="Magic Quarter",["s"]="The Magic Quarter is the northeastern district of the Undercity, serving as the center for Forsaken arcane study and dark spellcraft. Dominated by an ominous Temple of the Damned, the quarter houses practitioners of both the arcane and fel arts.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Occupying the northeastern quadrant of the subterranean city, the Magic Quarter is where the Forsaken preserve their arcane heritage and delve into darker methodologies. The centerpiece of the district is a looming Temple of the Damned, an architectural relic of Scourge design that has been repurposed by the free-willed undead. Beneath its vaulted, shadowy ceilings, mages practice subtle manipulations of magical energies alongside warlocks communing with demonic entities, making the quarter the nexus of intellectual power and occult research in Lordaeron.",["t"]="A Conclave of Dark Arts"},{["b"]="Beyond the study of raw evocation and summoning, the Magic Quarter functions as an essential civic hub for spellcasters. Portal trainers maintain transport links across Horde territories, while master tailors work with magically infused fabrics to craft robes and shrouds. Unlike Dalaran's strict segregation between academic wizardry and forbidden magic, the Forsaken blend arcane curiosity and fel power openly within these halls to secure their place against their many enemies.",["t"]="Scholars, Weavers, and Summoners"}}}}}
t["subzone:main-hall-northshire"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="22,334,18.494.0,37.202.0,30.208.0",["h"]="352c28",["n"]="Sala Principal (Villanorte)",["s"]="Sala Principal (Villanorte). La Sala Principal es la sala central de entrada de la Abadía de Villanorte en el Bosque de Elwynn. Sirve como la encrucijada principal que conecta los terrenos de la abadía con su torre superior, la Sala de Armas y el Ala de la Biblioteca. Aquí, los aventureros humanos recién reclutados se presentan para recibir sus asignaciones iniciales al servicio del Reino de Ventormenta. Cruzar los grandes arcos de la Abadía de Villanorte lleva a los visitantes directamente a la sala principal. Como núcleo central del edificio, canaliza a los aprendices y al personal clerical que llegan entre las distintas alas de la abadía: la marcial Sala de Armas a un lado, el ala de la biblioteca, dedicada al estudio, al otro y las escaleras que suben a la torre de la abadía. El tranquilo santuario de la sala se ve atenuado por el continuo conflicto en el valle, mientras los oficiales reúnen a los recién llegados capacitados para defender las fronteras del reino.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["race:Human"]="For humans of the kingdom, the Main Hall of Northshire Abbey marks the beginning of their journey in service of Stormwind and the Holy Light."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Main Hall serves as the central reception chamber and crossroads of Northshire Abbey. It directs recruits, priests, and visitors into the Hall of Arms, the Library Wing, and the abbey's upper tower.",["al"]={"what is main hall","northshire main hall use"},["q"]="What is the purpose of the Main Hall?"},{["a"]="Officers and clerics of the Stormwind defense stationed in the Main Hall evaluate incoming adventurers, providing them with their first marching orders to clear out threats encroaching on the abbey's grounds.",["al"]={"who gives quests here","abbey commander"},["q"]="Who directs new recruits here?"}},["kw"]={"abbey","elwynn","hall of arms","library wing","main hall","northshire","stormwind"},["n"]="Main Hall (Northshire)",["s"]="The Main Hall is the central entrance chamber of Northshire Abbey in Elwynn Forest. It serves as the primary crossroads connecting the abbey's grounds to its upper tower, the Hall of Arms, and the Library Wing. Here, newly recruited human adventurers report to receive their initial assignments in service of the Kingdom of Stormwind.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Stepping through the grand archways of Northshire Abbey brings visitors directly into the Main Hall. As the building's central hub, it channels arriving trainees and clerical staff between the abbey's distinct wings: the martial Hall of Arms on one side, the scholastic Library Wing on the other, and the stairs rising into the abbey tower. The quiet sanctuary of the hall is tempered by the ongoing strife in the valley, as officers rally able-bodied newcomers to defend the kingdom's borders.",["t"]="Heart of the Abbey"}}}}}
t["subzone:malaka-jin"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="10,305,17.479.0,25.373.0,19.227.0,24.169.0,27.211.0,30.203.0",["h"]="a7d729",["n"]="Malaka'jin",["s"]="Malaka'jin. Malaka'jin es un pequeño campamento de la Horda enclavado en las colinas bajas de Sierra Espolón, justo al sur de Poblado Tótem Siniestro. Habitado principalmente por cazadores trols de Lanza Negra, el asentamiento sirve como una rústica parada y puesto de caza para los viajeros que ascienden hacia los escarpados picos desde Los Baldíos. Escondido cerca del camino principal hacia Sierra Espolón, Malaka'jin ofrece un grato santuario para los caminantes de la Horda que se aventuran en las disputadas alturas. La aldea alberga a un grupo de curtidos cazadores trols que se ganan la vida entre los riscos y matorrales. A pesar de su vida modesta, estos cazadores ofrecen suministros, comercian con sus presas recién cazadas con los aventureros fatigados y vigilan con cautela a la hostil fauna montañosa y a los beligerantes tauren Tótem Siniestro que acechan más arriba por los senderos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Malaka'jin serves as the Horde's southernmost threshold in Stonetalon, offering a vital waystation on the trail between the Barrens and the northern mountain strongholds.",["race:Troll"]="For Darkspear trolls, Malaka'jin is a proud demonstration of troll self-reliance and tracking prowess, carving out a home in the rugged heights far from Kalimdor's tropical shores."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Malaka'jin is a small Horde village and outpost in the southern Stonetalon Mountains. It is inhabited by a community of Darkspear troll hunters who provide shelter, trade, and supplies to travelers climbing up from the Barrens.",["al"]={"where is malakajin","what is this place","malakajin stonetalon"},["q"]="What is Malaka'jin?"},{["a"]="The settlement is populated almost entirely by troll hunters. They sustain themselves by hunting the mountain game and trading meat and leather with passing adventurers.",["al"]={"malakajin npcs","who is here","trolls in stonetalon"},["q"]="Who lives in Malaka'jin?"},{["a"]="Aside from fierce mountain predators, the village is situated directly south of the hostile Grimtotem Post, leaving the small troll camp constantly vigilant against aggression from the antagonistic tauren tribe.",["al"]={"malakajin enemies","who attacks malakajin"},["q"]="What threats face the camp?"},{["a"]="No. In this era, Malaka'jin has no flight master. Adventurers traveling through the Stonetalon Mountains must rely on the flight master at Sun Rock Retreat further northwest or traverse the road on foot.",["al"]={"malakajin flight path","fly to malakajin"},["q"]="Is there a flight master here?"}},["kw"]={"darkspear","grimtotem","horde","hunters","malaka'jin","outpost","stonetalon","trolls"},["n"]="Malaka'jin",["s"]="Malaka'jin is a small Horde encampment nestled in the lower hills of the Stonetalon Mountains, just south of the Grimtotem Post. Inhabited primarily by Darkspear troll hunters, the settlement serves as a rustic waystation and hunting outpost for travelers ascending into the rugged peaks from the Barrens.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away near the main path into the Stonetalon Mountains, Malaka'jin provides a welcome sanctuary for Horde wanderers venturing into contested heights. The village is home to a band of rugged troll hunters who eke out a living off the crags and scrublands. While living modestly, these hunters offer supplies, trade their fresh game to weary adventurers, and keep a wary eye on the hostile mountain wildlife and the belligerent Grimtotem tauren lurking further up the trails.",["t"]="A Hunters' Refuge"},{["b"]="Perched precariously near the boundary of the Barrens, Malaka'jin marks one of the earliest Horde presences established in Stonetalon. Though small and quiet compared to the major fortress at Sun Rock Retreat further north, it functions as a vital logistical anchor, allowing Horde trackers to monitor tribal unrest and secure the winding roads against encroaching threats.",["t"]="A Foothold in the Heights"}}}}}
t["subzone:malden-s-orchard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,362,18.448.0,22.486.1,15.174.0,33.159.0,34.186.0,48.140.0",["h"]="68cc41",["n"]="Huerta de Malden",["s"]="Huerta de Malden. La Huerta de Malden es una granja en ruinas situada en el norte del Bosque de Argénteos, llamada así por el propietario humano que huyó durante la invasión de la Plaga en Lordaeron. Abandonada desde hace mucho tiempo, sus oscuros árboles de hoja perenne crecen descontrolados mientras feroces huargos negros acechan los terrenos. La derruida cabaña de la huerta sirvió de refugio temporal para un explorador Renegado que quedó aislado de su unidad. Antes de la Tercera Guerra, esta hacienda suministraba fruta fresca a las ciudades de Lordaeron, cuidada por un granjero llamado Malden. Cuando la Plaga arrasó el reino, Malden abandonó sus tierras para huir de la peste. En los años transcurridos desde entonces, la huerta ha quedado asfixiada bajo las densas y oscuras nieblas del Bosque de Argénteos. Los árboles de hoja perenne permanecen sin podar y sus frutos se pudren sin recoger en ramas marchitas, dejando el terreno completamente dominado por depredadores salvajes.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Horde"]="Travelers moving south from the Sepulcher or the Tirisfal border must tread carefully around the orchard due to the aggressive worg packs nesting on the farm.",["race:Undead"]="For the Forsaken, the orchard is a reminder of human ruin and a contested piece of northern Silverpine that Deathstalker scouts must secure against feral beasts."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Malden was a human farmer who lived here before the fall of Lordaeron. He abandoned the orchard and fled for his life when the Scourge invaded the realm during the Third War.",["al"]={"malden lore","who owned the orchard","who is malden"},["q"]="Who was Malden?"},{["a"]="With no living tenders to defend the farmstead, wild black worgs prowling Silverpine Forest claimed the dense grove and abandoned yard as their pack territory.",["al"]={"why are there worgs here","malden orchard dogs","worg infestation"},["q"]="Why is the orchard full of worgs?"},{["a"]="Deathstalker Erland McKree was trapped inside the cottage. Sent on a reconnaissance mission by the Forsaken, he was ambushed by the orchard's worgs and holed up inside until aid arrived.",["al"]={"cottage scout","who is in the house","deathstalker in the cabin"},["q"]="Who is trapped inside the cottage?"},{["a"]="No. The dark trees have not been tended in years, and their fruit rots on the branches amidst the decay spreading through Silverpine Forest.",["al"]={"is the fruit edible","malden's orchard harvest","can you pick fruit"},["q"]="Does anyone harvest fruit from this orchard now?"}},["kw"]={"cottage","erland mckree","ivar patch","malden","malden's orchard","maldens orchard","silverpine","worgs"},["n"]="Malden's Orchard",["s"]="Malden's Orchard is a ruined farmstead in northern Silverpine Forest, named after the human owner who fled during the Scourge invasion of Lordaeron. Long abandoned, its dark evergreen trees sit overgrown while vicious black worgs stalk the grounds. The orchard's crumbling cottage served as a temporary refuge for a stranded Forsaken scout cut off from his unit.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Before the Third War, this homestead supplied fresh fruit to the towns of Lordaeron, tended by a farmer named Malden. When the Scourge tore through the kingdom, Malden abandoned his land to flee the plague. In the years since, the orchard has choked under the dark, encroaching mists of Silverpine Forest. The evergreen trees remain unpruned and their fruit rots ungathered on blighted boughs, leaving the plot entirely reclaimed by wild predators.",["t"]="A Blighted Harvest"},{["b"]="The overgrown orchard has become a hunting ground for territorial black worgs, making it a hazardous route through northern Silverpine. During a reconnaissance mission for the Deathstalkers, the scout Erland McKree was dispatched to survey the area but found himself overwhelmed by the beasts. Pinned inside Malden's dilapidated cottage for days, Erland survived only until Forsaken reinforcements could break through the pack and escort him back to his fellow scouts at the Ivar Patch.",["t"]="Trapped in the Cottage"}}}}}
t["subzone:manor-mistmantle"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="16,239,20.393.0,24.491.1,34.132.0,30.115.1,27.177.0,42.173.1",["h"]="792946",["n"]="Mansión Mantoniebla",["s"]="Mansión Mantoniebla. La Mansión Mantoniebla es una hacienda en decadencia ubicada en las sombrías colinas del noreste del Bosque del Ocaso, al norte de Villa Oscura. Antaño un respetable hogar familiar, ha caído en la ruina y el horror, atestada de necrófagos no-muertos vinculados a su infame amo. Situada al oeste del Refugio de los Mendigos, la Mansión Mantoniebla se alza como un sombrío monumento al asesinato y la locura. Los terrenos están consumidos por la podredumbre y acechados por despiadados necrófagos que defienden la estructura en ruinas. En medio de la putrefacción y la vegetación marchita, el único signo de belleza viva en toda la propiedad es una flor solitaria y melancólica que crece en el jardín descuidado: la flor conocida como la Lágrima de Tilloa.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,1,0,1},["sec"]={0,1}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance investigators tracking the grim fate of the Moonbrook and Goldshire victims, Manor Mistmantle is the tragic final destination of the Legend of Stalvan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Manor Mistmantle lies in the northeastern reaches of Duskwood, situated directly north of Darkshire and just west of Beggar's Haunt.",["al"]={"manor mistmantle location","where is mistmantle manor","how to find manor mistmantle"},["q"]="Where is Manor Mistmantle located?"},{["a"]="The estate belongs to Stalvan Mistmantle, a former tutor who now exists as an undead creature surrounded by ghouls.",["al"]={"who is in mistmantle manor","manor mistmantle boss","stalvan house"},["q"]="Who lives in Manor Mistmantle?"},{["a"]="The Tear of Tilloa is a solitary, delicate flower blooming in the garden of Manor Mistmantle, standing out as the only surviving sign of natural life amidst the decayed grounds.",["al"]={"tear of tilloa flower","mistmantle garden flower","tilloa flower"},["q"]="What is the Tear of Tilloa?"},{["a"]="The ghouls roaming the manor grounds are minions bound to Stalvan Mistmantle, serving to protect their master and slaughter anyone who dares trespass on his blighted estate.",["al"]={"why are ghouls at mistmantle","mistmantle undead","manor mistmantle enemies"},["q"]="Why are there undead guarding the grounds?"}},["kw"]={"beggar's haunt","darkshire","duskwood","ghouls","manor mistmantle","stalvan","stalvan mistmantle","tear of tilloa"},["n"]="Manor Mistmantle",["s"]="Manor Mistmantle is a decaying estate nestled in the shadowed hills of northeastern Duskwood, north of Darkshire. Once a proper family homestead, it has fallen into ruin and horror, crawling with undead ghouls bound to its infamous master.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Located west of Beggar's Haunt, Manor Mistmantle stands as a grim monument to murder and madness. The grounds are choked with decay and prowled by vicious ghouls who defend the ruined structure. Amidst the rot and withered vegetation, the only sign of living beauty on the entire property is a solitary, sorrowful blossom growing in the untended garden: the flower known as the Tear of Tilloa.",["t"]="A Blighted Homestead"},{["b"]="The manor belongs to Stalvan Mistmantle, a former schoolteacher and private tutor whose horrific crimes in Moonbrook and Goldshire became the stuff of dark legend across the kingdom. Now an agent of the undead, Stalvan lurks in the upper floor of his family home, surrounded by remnants of his slaughtered victims and guarded by shambling horrors. Travelers and investigators from Darkshire frequently find that the trail of Duskwood's most notorious phantom ends at this blood-soaked manor.",["t"]="The Master of the Estate"}}}}}
t["subzone:menethil-harbor"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="15,461,22.571.0,28.516.0,46.228.0,26.258.0,31.231.0,44.285.0",["h"]="f0c83a",["n"]="Puerto de Menethil",["s"]="Puerto de Menethil. El Puerto de Menethil es una ciudad portuaria enana fuertemente fortificada, situada en una isla frente a la costa occidental de Los Humedales. Construida sobre un antiguo astillero orco y bautizada en honor al rey Terenas Menethil II, sirve como la principal arteria marítima que conecta los Reinos del Este con las distantes costas de Kalimdor. Al abrigo de enormes almenas de piedra y de las robustas torres del Castillo de Menethil, es un bullicioso punto de encuentro para mercaderes, soldados de permiso y curtidos aventureros. El emplazamiento del Puerto de Menethil sirvió por primera vez al Jefe de Guerra Orgrim Martillo Maldito durante la Segunda Guerra, cuando la Horda construyó una armada de invasión con madera y hierro saqueados de Khaz Modan. Tras la derrota de los orcos, el Gran Almirante Daelin Valiente supervisó la reconstrucción del fondeadero para convertirlo en un refugio de primer orden para la Alianza, dándole nombre como tributo al difunto rey Terenas Menethil II de Lordaeron. A pesar de su remota ubicación pantanosa, sigue siendo un bastión fuertemente defendido, reforzado por murallas colosales, una única calzada con puente y las cuatro torres de vigilancia de piedra del Castillo de Menethil.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="For any Alliance traveler journeying west, Menethil Harbor is the vital staging ground and sole maritime bridge linking the Eastern Kingdoms to Theramore and Kalimdor.",["race:Dwarf"]="Though bearing a human king's name, this port is maintained primarily by dwarven stonework and manned by Ironforge guards holding the outer threshold of Khaz Modan."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Vessels departing the docks of Menethil Harbor cross the Great Sea to the continent of Kalimdor. Scheduled passenger ships run regular routes to Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and north to the night elven haven of Auberdine.",["al"]={"menethil harbor boat","where does the boat go","menethil ferries","kalimdor boats"},["q"]="Where do the ships in Menethil Harbor sail to?"},{["a"]="Menethil Harbor operates as an Alliance settlement under the authority of Ironforge. Captain Stoutfist commands the town guard and coordinates harbor defense out of Menethil Keep, keeping the docks secure from swamp beasts, renegade orcs, and inland raiders.",["al"]={"who is in charge of menethil","menethil harbor leader","who leads menethil"},["q"]="Who rules Menethil Harbor?"},{["a"]="The harbor was named by Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore after the Second War in tribute to King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron, whose leadership united the human, dwarven, and elven realms into the original Alliance of Lordaeron.",["al"]={"why menethil harbor","menethil name origin","who is menethil"},["q"]="Why is the town named Menethil?"},{["a"]="The harbor faces persistent danger from the Dragonmaw clan lurking in the Wetlands hills, who regularly try to cut off the pass through Dun Algaz to starve the port of reinforcements. Dark Iron incursions to the north near Dun Modr and marauding raptors add to the garrison's troubles.",["al"]={"is menethil harbor in danger","menethil threats","wetlands orcs menethil"},["q"]="What threats does the harbor face right now?"}},["kw"]={"auberdine","boat","deepwater","docks","ferry","harbor","menethil","stoutfist","theramore","wetlands"},["n"]="Menethil Harbor",["s"]="Menethil Harbor is a heavily fortified dwarven port town perched on an island off the western shore of the Wetlands. Built over an old Orcish shipyard and named after King Terenas Menethil II, it acts as the primary maritime lifeline connecting the Eastern Kingdoms to the distant shores of Kalimdor. Sheltered behind massive stone battlements and the sturdy towers of Menethil Keep, it is a bustling hub for merchants, off-duty soldiers, and salty adventurers.",["sec"]={{["b"]="The site of Menethil Harbor first served Warchief Orgrim Doomhammer during the Second War, when the Horde constructed an invasion armada out of timber and iron ransacked from Khaz Modan. After the orcs were routed, Grand Admiral Daelin Proudmoore oversaw the rebuilding of the anchorage into a premier Alliance haven, naming it in tribute to the late King Terenas Menethil II of Lordaeron. Despite its remote marshland setting, it remains a heavily defended bastion, reinforced by massive walls, a single bridged causeway, and the four stone watchtowers of Menethil Keep.",["t"]="A Port Carved from War"},{["b"]="Today, the harbor is the grand crossroads of the Alliance. Ships steam continually across the ocean toward Theramore Isle in Dustwallow Marsh and Auberdine in darkshore, carrying trade, diplomats, and off-duty Kul Tiran marines blowing their wages at the Deepwater Tavern. Yet peace is fragile here: inland supply paths through Dun Algaz are regularly contested by the Dragonmaw clan, while hostile Dark Iron raiders pressure the northern marshes, leaving Captain Stoutfist and the harbor garrison on constant alert.",["t"]="Gateway Across the Great Sea"}}}}}
t["subzone:merchant-coast"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,248,35.506.0,36.200.0,49.201.0,37.222.0",["h"]="3c2c2e",["n"]="La Costa Mercante",["s"]="La Costa Mercante. La Costa Mercante es el tramo del litoral oriental de Los Baldíos que bordea el Mare Magnum. Dominada por el bullicioso puerto goblin de Trinquete, la costa debe su nombre al lucrativo comercio marítimo, aunque los piratas se la disputan constantemente. A lo largo del borde oriental de Los Baldíos, La Costa Mercante sirve como una arteria marítima vital que conecta el centro de Kalimdor con los Reinos del Este y Theramore. Su nombre rinde homenaje a los laboriosos comerciantes goblins del Cártel Bonvapor, cuyo puerto neutral de Trinquete gestiona cargamentos para cualquiera que disponga de monedas. Sin embargo, las rutas marítimas abiertas atraen a algo más que navíos mercantes: los filibusteros del Mar del Sur merodean por las arenas y las aguas cercanas, acechando a los barcos mercantes y estableciendo operaciones ilícitas a lo largo de las playas.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["faction:Alliance"]="The Alliance maintains a nearby naval presence at Northwatch Hold, keeping a wary eye on both the goblin trade passing through Ratchet and the unruly Southsea pirates along the shore.",["faction:Horde"]="The Merchant Coast is the Horde's primary commercial lifeline to the sea in the Barrens, making the security of Ratchet and suppression of local pirates vital for regional supply lines."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The shoreline earned its name from the lucrative trade conducted through the goblin port of Ratchet. Steamwheedle merchants move cargo across the Great Sea from this coast to ports all around Azeroth.",["al"]={"merchant coast name origin","why called merchant coast"},["q"]="Why is it called the Merchant Coast?"},{["a"]="The most prominent settlement is Ratchet, a neutral goblin port city run by Gazlowe. Farther south along the coast lies the Alliance stronghold of Northwatch Hold, while Fray Island sits just offshore.",["al"]={"towns on merchant coast","what is on merchant coast"},["q"]="What major settlements are on the Merchant Coast?"},{["a"]="While Ratchet controls the immediate harbor, the Southsea Freebooters have established encampments along the surrounding beaches. These pirates actively disrupt trade, rob goblin convoys, and challenge Ratchet's authority.",["al"]={"pirates on merchant coast","who is attacking merchant coast"},["q"]="Who controls the beaches around here?"}},["kw"]={"barrens","great sea","merchant coast","ratchet","southsea freebooters","steamwheedle cartel"},["n"]="Merchant Coast",["s"]="The Merchant Coast is the stretch of eastern shoreline in the Barrens bordering the Great Sea. Dominated by the bustling goblin port of Ratchet, the coast derives its name from lucrative sea trade, though it remains constantly contested by pirates.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Running along the eastern edge of the Barrens, the Merchant Coast serves as a vital maritime artery connecting central Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms and Theramore. Its name honors the industrious goblin traders of the Steamwheedle Cartel, whose neutral port of Ratchet handles cargo for anyone with coin. However, the open sea lanes attract more than merchant vessels: Southsea Freebooters prowl the sands and nearby waters, preying on merchant ships and setting up illicit operations along the beaches.",["t"]="A Gateway for Commerce and Conflict"}}}}}
t["subzone:military-ward"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="13,282,26.548.0,31.342.0,26.158.0,42.150.0,37.166.0,41.179.0",["h"]="235709",["n"]="Sala Militar",["s"]="Sala Militar. La Sala Militar sirve como el corazón marcial de Forjaz, albergando la infraestructura de mando de la ciudad, maestros de armas y barracones. Marcado por llamativos estandartes rojos, es el lugar donde los soldados, cazadores e ingenieros de asedio enanos entrenan junto a máquinas de asedio mecanizadas y máquinas voladoras. Situada en el perímetro norte de la fortaleza de la montaña, la Sala Militar concentra las fuerzas defensivas de Forjaz en una bulliciosa zona de concentración. El complejo central, la Sala de Armas, acoge a instructores de guerreros y cazadores, maestros de batalla y hangares que albergan máquinas voladoras y tanques de vapor enanos. Alrededor de las plazas de instrucción y los muñecos de entrenamiento se encuentran puntos de suministros como Armaduras de Placas y Malla de Craghelm, Suministros de Caza de Goldfury y Armería Timberline, lo que convierte al distrito en el principal punto de preparación para los montañeros y defensores de la ciudad.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Hunter"]="Rangers and mountaineers will find beast masters and supplies in the Hall of Arms, alongside Goldfury's Hunting Supplies for munitions and gear.",["class:Warrior"]="The Military Ward is the chief martial hub in Ironforge, offering warrior trainers, training dummies for combat practice, and weapon masters to broaden your battlefield arsenal."},["faq"]={{["a"]="It is the martial quarter of Ironforge, serving as the central base for the dwarven army, warrior and hunter trainers, weapons merchants, and siege machinery.",["al"]={"military ward ironforge","ironforge barracks","ironforge warrior district"},["q"]="What is the Military Ward?"},{["a"]="Weapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand is stationed at Timberline Arms within the Military Ward, offering training in various armaments to Alliance fighters.",["al"]={"ironforge weapon master","where is buliwyf stonehand","learn weapons ironforge"},["q"]="Where can I train in weapons in Ironforge?"},{["a"]="The Hall of Arms functions as the military headquarters, containing combat instructors, battlemasters, and large bays storing steam tanks and dwarven flying machines.",["al"]={"hall of arms ironforge","what is in hall of arms","ironforge siege engines"},["q"]="What is kept inside the Hall of Arms?"},{["a"]="Ironforge's districts use specific heraldic colors for navigation and tradition; the Military Ward is draped in bold red banners to represent the martial arm of the mountain city.",["al"]={"military ward colors","red banners ironforge"},["q"]="Why are the banners red in this district?"}},["kw"]={"buliwyf stonehand","flying machines","hall of arms","ironforge","military ward","steam tanks","timberline arms"},["n"]="Military Ward",["s"]="The Military Ward serves as the martial heart of Ironforge, housing the city's command infrastructure, weapons masters, and barracks. Marked by bold red banners, it is where dwarven soldiers, hunters, and siege engineers train alongside mechanized siege engines and flying machines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated within the northern perimeter of the mountain fortress, the Military Ward concentrates Ironforge's defensive forces into a bustling staging ground. The central complex, the Hall of Arms, accommodates warrior and hunter trainers, battlemasters, and hangars housing dwarven flying machines and steam tanks. Surrounding the drill squares and training dummies are supply outlets such as Craghelm's Plate and Chain, Goldfury's Hunting Supplies, and Timberline Arms, making the ward the primary staging point for mountaineers and city defenders.",["t"]="The Anvil of Dwarven Might"},{["b"]="Distinguished from the pale blue of the Commons and the fiery orange of the Great Forge, the Military Ward is draped in martial red banners. Between drills and weapons inspections, soldiers and off-duty guards gather at Bruuk's Corner for an ale, while Weapon Master Buliwyf Stonehand instructs recruits in ancient dwarven martial traditions.",["t"]="A Garrison under Banners of War"}}}}}
t["subzone:mirage-raceway"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="14,445,24.616.0,20.473.0,27.200.0,24.197.0,42.191.0,31.191.0",["h"]="166897",["n"]="Circuito del Espejismo",["s"]="Circuito del Espejismo. El Circuito del Espejismo es un campo de pruebas de ingeniería improvisado situado en las resplandecientes salinas de Las Mil Agujas. Fundado a raíz de la enconada rivalidad entre el manitas goblin Pozík y el ingeniero gnomo Fizzle Pernolatón, enfrenta a coches cohete de gran velocidad entre sí a través de la tierra cuarteada. La pista sirve como un punto de encuentro neutral donde miembros tanto de la Alianza como de la Horda acuden a apostar, cacharrear y animar a sus máquinas favoritas. Extendido a lo largo del vasto suelo del desierto blanco de El Desierto de Sal, el Circuito del Espejismo nació de un implacable duelo de rencores entre dos maestros manitas: el goblin Pozík y el gnomo Fizzle Pernolatón. Decididos a resolver de una vez por todas qué raza posee una inventiva técnica superior, ambos construyeron coches de aceleración personalizados propulsados por cohetes y reclutaron a cuadrillas rivales para enfrentarlos entre sí en duelos diarios a gran velocidad. La incesante competición ha convertido las llanuras yermas en un bullicioso centro neurálgico de invención, sabotaje y pruebas, en el que cada cuadrilla busca desesperadamente cualquier ventaja mecánica.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0,0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["profession:Engineering"]="For tinkerers of any faction, the Raceway represents the ultimate clash between goblin risk-taking and gnomish meticulous design, offering field tests of raw speed, volatile fuel, and experimental vehicle parts.",["race:Gnome"]="Fizzle Brassbolts flies the banner of Gnomeregan here, relying on fellow gnomes and allies to prove that disciplined innovation easily outperforms reckless goblin combustion."},["faq"]={{["a"]="The Mirage Raceway is an open-air rocket-car drag strip laid across the salt flats of Thousand Needles. It was built by rival engineers seeking to prove whether goblin or gnome mechanics are superior.",["al"]={"what is mirage raceway","raceway purpose","shimmering flats track"},["q"]="What is the Mirage Raceway?"},{["a"]="The track is maintained jointly by the gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts and the goblin tinkerer Pozzik. Each operates a dedicated crew and workshop along the raceway to field competing rocket cars.",["al"]={"who leads raceway","fizzle and pozzik","who built this track"},["q"]="Who runs the races here?"},{["a"]="Yes. The raceway operates under an informal neutral truce so that both factions can visit the camps, place wagers, aid the rival engineering crews, and purchase supplies without interference.",["al"]={"is mirage raceway neutral","can alliance visit","can horde visit"},["q"]="Can Horde and Alliance both use this area?"},{["a"]="The flat, wide expanse of the Shimmering Flats provides a smooth, unobstructed surface ideal for rocket-propelled vehicles that require miles of room to reach top speeds and safely slow down.",["al"]={"why thousand needles","why race on salt","why in shimmering flats"},["q"]="Why race out in the salt flats?"}},["kw"]={"fizzle brassbolts","mirage raceway","pozzik","rocket car","shimmering flats","thousand needles"},["n"]="Mirage Raceway",["s"]="The Mirage Raceway is an impromptu engineering proving ground situated in the shimmering salt flats of Thousand Needles. Founded on the heated rivalry between goblin tinkerer Pozzik and gnome engineer Fizzle Brassbolts, it pits high-speed rocket cars against one another across the baked earth. The track serves as a neutral gathering place where members of both the Alliance and Horde come to wager, tinker, and cheer on their favored machines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Sprawled across the vast white desert floor of the Shimmering Flats, the Mirage Raceway was born out of an unrelenting grudge match between two master tinkerers: the goblin Pozzik and the gnome Fizzle Brassbolts. Determined to settle once and for all whose race possesses superior technical ingenuity, the two constructed custom rocket-powered drag cars and recruited rival crews to pit them against each other in daily high-velocity showdowns. The relentless competition has turned the barren flats into a bustling hub of invention, sabotage, and testing as each crew desperately looks for any mechanical advantage.",["t"]="Speed, Salt, and Rivalry"},{["b"]="Because both teams need supplies, fuel, and test pilots, the raceway maintains an uneasy truce between the Horde and Alliance. Spectators gather from across Kalimdor to cheer on either gnome precision or goblin firepower, while gamblers and shady opportunists thrive on the constant wagers placed on the results. Beyond the roar of rocket thrusters, the camps serve as a busy trading depot for travelers journeying between Thousand Needles and the blazing sands of Tanaris.",["t"]="A Neutral Crossroads"}}}}}
t["subzone:mirror-lake"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="11,296,15.590.0,29.236.0,35.262.0,50.177.0",["h"]="0fa422",["n"]="Lago Espejo",["s"]="Lago Espejo. El Lago Espejo es una pintoresca masa de agua resguardada en el noroeste del Bosque de Elwynn, cerca de un huerto de frutales. Alimentado por una suave cascada bajo los acantilados de Ventormenta, su tranquila superficie oculta los peligros que acechan en sus orillas, desde bandidos Defias al acecho hasta extrañas perturbaciones en las líneas Ley locales. Situado bajo las imponentes murallas de la Ciudad de Ventormenta, el Lago Espejo debería ser un pacífico retiro para pescadores y viajeros cansados. En su lugar, los forajidos de la Hermandad Defias merodean por los huertos circundantes, convirtiendo cualquier estancia prolongada en un peligro para los lugareños que pasan por allí. Peor aún, las perturbaciones místicas por todo Azeroth han comenzado a distorsionar los canales naturales de energía arcana por todo el bosque. Los magos del Sagrario del Mago vigilan el lago con cautela y envían practicantes para tomar muestras de sus corrientes y asegurarse de que las comunidades río abajo no se envenenen con los vertidos arcanos caóticos.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Mage"]="Initiates studying under the Wizard's Sanctum in Stormwind are dispatched here to gather water samples, learning firsthand how turbulent arcane channels can seep into the natural ecosystem.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though close to the capital's towering walls, the lake stands as a reminder of how thinly stretched the kingdom's guards are against Defias outlaws."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Despite its scenic appearance, the area around the lake is heavily prowled by Defias bandits who target travelers and farmers. Additionally, the recent fluctuations in regional magic have prompted concerns about the lake's water safety.",["al"]={"is mirror lake safe","mirror lake enemies","defias mirror lake"},["q"]="Why is Mirror Lake dangerous?"},{["a"]="Massive magical conflicts across Azeroth have destabilized ley currents throughout Elwynn Forest and Stormwind. The Wizard's Sanctum dispatches initiates to sample the lake's water to test for unstable arcane residue before it can affect those who drink from it.",["al"]={"wizard sanctum mirror lake","mirror lake quest","magic in mirror lake"},["q"]="Why are mages studying Mirror Lake?"},{["a"]="The waterfall cascades down from the high cliffs and waterways flanking the perimeter of Stormwind City, feeding the lake before the water winds through the Elwynn river system.",["al"]={"mirror lake waterfall","water source mirror lake"},["q"]="Where does the waterfall at Mirror Lake come from?"}},["kw"]={"defias","elwynn forest","mirror lake","stormwind","waterfall","wizards sanctum"},["n"]="Mirror Lake",["s"]="Mirror Lake is a picturesque body of water tucked into northwestern Elwynn Forest near an orchard. Fed by a gentle waterfall beneath the cliffs of Stormwind, its tranquil surface belies the dangers lurking on its shores, from prowling Defias bandits to strange disruptions in the local ley lines.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Situated beneath the towering ramparts of Stormwind City, Mirror Lake ought to be a peaceful retreat for fishermen and weary travelers. Instead, brigands of the Defias Brotherhood stalk the surrounding orchards, making any prolonged stay perilous for passing locals. Worse still, mystical disturbances across Azeroth have begun warping the natural channels of arcane energy throughout the forest. The mages of the Wizard's Sanctum keep a cautious eye on the lake, sending practitioners to sample its currents and ensure that downstream communities are not poisoned by chaotic arcane runoff.",["t"]="A Troubled Idyl"}}}}}
t["subzone:mirror-lake-orchard"] = {["faq"]={},["fp"]="19,281,21.494.0,43.208.0,37.161.0,43.283.0,61.185.0",["h"]="61e298",["n"]="Vergel del Lago Espejo",["s"]="Vergel del Lago Espejo. El Vergel del Lago Espejo es una tranquila arboleda y cabaña situada en la orilla sur del Lago Espejo, en el oeste del Bosque de Elwynn. En su día fue una apacible granja cerca de las Cataratas del Trueno, pero ha caído en manos de los bandidos Defias, que se aprovechan de la campiña mientras los guardias de Ventormenta miran hacia otro lado. Escondido cerca de las aguas torrenciales de las Cataratas del Trueno, el Vergel del Lago Espejo fue en su momento una productiva granja que se beneficiaba de las aguas limpias del Lago Espejo. Hoy en día, la apacible cabaña se encuentra invadida, tomada por ladrones y forajidos oportunistas que portan los colores de la Hermandad Defias. Con las fuerzas militares del reino mermadas y el rey Varian Wrynn desaparecido, las propiedades rurales como este vergel se han convertido en presas fáciles para los forajidos que buscan asegurarse escondites por toda la campiña de Elwynn.",["sec"]={},["source"]={["sp"]={["faq"]={0,0,0,0},["sec"]={0}},["text"]={["ang"]={["class:Rogue"]="The orchard demonstrates classic Defias strategy: seizing defensible, overlooked properties near water and cliffs to monitor roads while evading city patrols.",["faction:Alliance"]="For Alliance travelers, the occupied orchard is another bitter sign of the Defias Brotherhood's bold expansion across the heartland of the kingdom."},["faq"]={{["a"]="Defias bandits currently occupy Mirror Lake Orchard and the cottage alongside it. They have driven away whatever honest folk once tended the trees and now use the secluded grounds as a base in western Elwynn.",["al"]={"who is at mirror lake orchard","who lives here","orchard enemies"},["q"]="Who controls Mirror Lake Orchard right now?"},{["a"]="The orchard sits along the southern shore of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest, just east of Thunder Falls and north of the main road heading toward Westfall.",["al"]={"mirror lake orchard location","where is the orchard","find orchard elwynn"},["q"]="Where is Mirror Lake Orchard located?"},{["a"]="Stormwind's standing army is largely absent from rural Elwynn due to political deadlock and the mysterious disappearance of King Varian Wrynn. With local garrisons shorthanded, distant farmsteads and orchards are frequently left to fend for themselves against the Defias Brotherhood.",["al"]={"why are defias here","where are the guards"},["q"]="Why hasn't Stormwind reclaimed the orchard?"},{["a"]="Mirror Lake drains directly into Thunder Falls, placing the orchard just above the roaring cascade. Its secluded position near the cliffs makes it an ideal, defensible spot for bandits.",["al"]={"thunder falls connection","orchard and waterfall"},["q"]="What is the connection between the orchard and Thunder Falls?"}},["kw"]={"defias brotherhood","elwynn forest","mirror lake","mirror lake orchard","stormwind bandits","thunder falls"},["n"]="Mirror Lake Orchard",["s"]="Mirror Lake Orchard is a quiet grove and cottage nestled on the southern banks of Mirror Lake in western Elwynn Forest. Once a peaceful homestead near Thunder Falls, it has fallen into the hands of Defias bandits who exploit the countryside while Stormwind's guards look elsewhere.",["sec"]={{["b"]="Tucked away near the cascading waters of Thunder Falls, Mirror Lake Orchard was once a productive farmstead benefiting from the clean waters of Mirror Lake. Today, the peaceful cottage sits overrun, claimed by opportunistic thieves and brigands flying the colors of the Defias Brotherhood. With the kingdom's military stretched thin and King Varian Wrynn missing, rural properties like this orchard have become easy pickings for outlaws looking to secure hideouts across the Elwynn countryside.",["t"]="A Grove Under Seizure"}}}}}
